this skill exists\nAll four audits independently converged on the SAME spine (8 dimensions → P0/P1/P2 → AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT → adversarial verification) and got burned by the SAME mistakes. This skill bakes in the spine and the scar tissue so future audits finish in fewer sittings and don't repeat the token furnaces.\n\n## Non-negotiables (every audit lost real tokens ignoring at least one)\n1. **Cheap orientation BEFORE any agent fan-out.** A wide parallel swarm of file-reading agents is the #1 token-torch (TPP: 22 agents / 95 min / **0 output files**; TMP: >3M tokens on stalling swarms). Start with bash: repo map, LOC by subsystem, a structural digest (TODO/duplication/complexity), `git` branch state, CI status, `pytest --collect-only`. Only fan out AFTER you know the shape.\n2. **Prefer the Orchestrator over same-family subagents.** Offload reading / summarizing / searching to cheap local agents (`dispatcher.py offload --agent <gemini|cursor|vibe>`); keep only synthesis and hard judgment in the lead seat. Cap parallel agents ≈4–6, **path-scope every prompt**, and require **disk-first artifacts**. Full routing in `reference/orchestration.md`.\n3. **On a Dropbox/synced or overloaded machine, local test red/green is NOT authoritative — CI is ground truth.** (TMP's gitignored golden CSVs read as cross-OS \"float drift\"; TPP reported \"49 vitest failures\" that were CI-green — just an overloaded box.) Confirm via CI or a non-synced checkout before any conclusion.\n4. **Check machine load + kill stale agents FIRST.** Leaked Claude-Code agent processes (TPP: **378**) masquerade as \"Dropbox is slow\" / \"Codex is clogging compute\" — and misattributing it burns hours and trust. `ps`, load average, run the reaper, THEN start jobs.\n5. **Disk-first artifacts.** Every analysis agent WRITES its findings to a file under `Code/Audits/<repo>/` (for example `<YYYY-MM-DD>-NN-<area>.md`) and returns only a short index + counts — never the full text. Prevents re-reading and context blowup, and is the continuity trail when the audit spans sessions.\n6. **Schema-less Markdown returns from subagents.** Strict `StructuredOutput` schemas broke most subagents across these audits (and the \"deep-research\" swarm). Ask for Markdown.\n7. **Adversarially verify every finding before filing.** Re-check each against the live tip; drop already-implemented ones (mark `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`). Real bugs routinely **pass the existing test suite** (homogeneous fixtures hide them) — verify the logic, not the green check.\n8. **Audit agents are READ-ONLY.** They drifted into editing code mid-audit (Counter_Risk). State it in every prompt; diff-scan for unexpected modifications before banking anything.\n9. **Store audit continuity outside the audited repo.** Canonical artifacts go under `/Users/teacher/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Audits/<repo>/`, with `AUDIT_LEDGER.md` updated at start, completion, issue filing, PR creation, merge, and follow-up verification. Only mirror into `docs/audit/` or `docs/ux-review/` when the repo itself intentionally owns an in-repo log.\n10. **UX/design findings must be observed.** For any UI/operator surface, use the UX overlay: rendered browser output, `frontend_verify.py` snapshots, screenshots, driven scenarios, the `ux_review.py` panel, and mined improvement hints. Do not score usability from code reading alone.\n\n## Orchestrator capability consult (optional, non-blocking)\n\nConsult **once per phase**, not once per audit. This audit is six phases and the capabilities that\napply differ sharply between them; asking once at the start returns a set that is wrong for five of\nthe six. Pass the phase as the surface:\n\n**Send one of these FOURTEEN literal strings and nothing else.** `surface` resolves by PREFIX, so an\nunsubstituted template like `repo-audit:phase-N` or `repo-audit:dimension-N` does **not** error — it\nresolves to `repo-audit`'s surface-wide set alone, returning ONE capability where the phase declares\nthree or four, with nothing in the answer to say it went wrong. Measured 2026-08-23: three audits\nunder identical instructions consulted 13, 9 and 2 distinct surfaces. The advisor now reports a\n`surface_template` field and prints `!! SURFACE LOOKS LIKE AN UNSUBSTITUTED TEMPLATE` when it sees\none — if you get that line, substitute the real value and re-ask.\n\n| surface to pass (copy verbatim) | what it binds |\n|---|---|\n| `repo-audit:phase-1` | **nothing, deliberately** — the playbook says bash only, NO agents |\n| `repo-audit:phase-2` | decomposing the 8 dimensions, per-repo conventions — this is the SPLITTER context |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-1` | the surface-wide offload only — d1 finds defects; the proof is phase 4 |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-2` | the consolidation campaign (duplication, root-vs-template drift) |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-3` | the wiring/direction checks (config key → loader → consumer) |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-4` | the frontend gate plus the panel's adversarial critic |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-5` | the offload the playbook names outright for public-field research |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-6` | the reusable-structure scan (`feature_scan`) |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-7` | the surface-wide offload only — d7 is cost/benefit research |\n| `repo-audit:dimension-8` | the capability audit surfaces — can-fire, did-fire, was-it-worth-firing, held switches |\n| `repo-audit:phase-3` | adversarial verification, and partitioned review — the phase disposes N candidate findings against the live tip, which is that module's corpus shape |\n| `repo-audit:phase-4` | the named test gate + deliberate-break proof, triage for prioritisation |\n| `repo-audit:phase-5` | recording which capabilities actually helped |\n| `repo-audit:fix` | campaign, epic, coverage work in the follow-up arc |\n\nPass the `repo-audit:dimension-<literal>` row in that dimension AGENT's own prompt — a worker is its\nown context and deliberately does not inherit the splitter's capabilities.\n\nPhase 2 fans out to eight bounded dimension agents, so each agent gets its own surface — the eight\n`repo-audit:dimension-*` rows above, one per agent. Dimension 8 is the one that audits local skills\nand automations, so it is where a surface's own missed capabilities show up.\n\n**Always pass `repository` and `repo_path` as well.** They are what let a capability's declared\nprecondition be EVALUATED instead of investigated: `repository` is the `owner/name` under audit (e.g.\n`stranske/Workflows`), `repo_path` an absolute path to its checkout. Measured cost of omitting them:\n`frontend-verifier` was offered to two repositories with **zero application UI** across three audit\nrounds and declined every time as \"the binding's own precondition is never evaluated\" — the probe, the\ndeclaration and both parameters existed, and nothing supplied them. With them supplied the same offer\ncomes back `PRECONDITION NOT MET: requires observable_surface and this repository has none`, plus any\nper-repo contraindication that repo's own record holds, so it is one line to dismiss instead of a\ndimension to investigate. Neither field changes which capabilities are returned or their order — the\naxis annotates only. If you omit them the answer says `?? PRECONDITION(S) NOT EVALUATED` and names\nexactly what to re-ask with; do that rather than reasoning around it.\n\nCall `mcp__orchestrator__capability_advice` with `skill: \"repo-audit\"`, `surface: \"<one literal row\nfrom the table above>\"` — for example `surface: \"repo-audit:phase-3\"` or\n`surface: \"repo-audit:dimension-4\"`, and never the template string `repo-audit:phase-N` —\nplus `repository` and `repo_path` for the repo under audit,\nand **the user's own wording of the work in front of you** — never this skill's name or description\n(identical text every time would make the learned association an artifact of the prompt rather than\nof the work). The declared binding answers even when the wording does not classify, so a phase always\nreturns its set. If the tool is missing or errors, skip it and carry on: this skill never depends on it.\n\nWhen you use one, close the loop so the next audit's ordering is better than this one's:\n\n    python3 ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator/capability_propensity.py \\\n      trigger --capability <id> --experiment <experiment_id>\n    python3 ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator/capability_propensity.py \\\n      useful --capability <id> --experiment <experiment_id> --evidence '<what it CHANGED>'\n\n`--evidence` must name what the capability changed about the finding or the outcome; \"it ran\" is not\nusefulness and an unevidenced verdict is refused. Used none? Record nothing — a named-but-not-triggered\ncandidate is the control arm and is already captured.\n\n**Read each candidate's `how_to_use` field, not its `blocker`.** `blocker` describes the LANE's\nautomatic entry path and routinely reads \"matched but a gate blocked invocation\" for a capability you\ncan simply call; `how_to_use` gives the direct call and, where one exists, the **BOUNDARY** — what\nthat capability cannot take. `adversarial-review` was declined here as \"its matcher is closer_gate:\nhigh_stakes_review, a lane gate, not an audit dimension\" when the matcher is only how the closer lane\nenters it automatically, and `offload` was declined nine times in one run for work that had to be\nfirst-person — both answered by `how_to_use`, which the answer now carries.\n\nThe answer is **advice, not dispatch** — `dispatch_ready` is false for every capability today, so a\nmatch is a candidate to *consider*, never a thing to run. `useful: false` is a normal, common and\ncorrect answer: note it in one line and move on; never reword the task to force a match. Re-consult\nonly when the work changes shape, passing the prior result as `previous`.\n\n## Phase 0 — Scoping interview (do this FIRST, with the user)\nThe distinctive, per-repo part of every audit. Before any work, pin scope with `AskUserQuestion` (this exact step saved the Counter_Risk audit from auditing 222 files of vendored `.github` infra). Cover:\n- **Scope boundary** — app code only, or infra/CI/vendored too? Which dirs to EXCLUDE (`node_modules`, `.github`, synced-from-upstream files)? Auditing code that's synced/owned elsewhere yields non-actionable findings.\n- **Primary surfaces** — which entry points / UIs matter, and which is most \"ready\"?\n- **Verification depth** — run tests + builds, or static review only?\n- **Budget / fan-out tolerance** — generous-checkpointed vs. tight; how hard to parallelize.\n- **Deliverables** — report only? prioritized backlog? filed issues? PRs? (Default: report + backlog; file issues/PRs only when asked.)\n- **Repo-distinctive elements** — ASK the user what's unusual about THIS repo (hosting/deploy, build backend, test/lint conventions, domain), THEN load `reference/repo-distinctives.md` for the known per-repo gotchas and the general categories to probe. This is the \"interact about the unique elements before running the full audit\" step.\n\nRead `reference/audit-storage.md`, create/update the repo folder under `Code/Audits`, and write the answers to `<YYYY-MM-DD>-scope.md` or `<YYYY-MM-DD>-audit-run.md` there — it anchors the whole run and survives a context reset. If the repo already has an intentional in-repo audit log, link or mirror the concise summary rather than making the repo-local copy the source of truth.\n\n## Phases 1–5 — the standard audit (see `reference/playbook.md`)\n1. **Orient (cheap, bash-only).** Repo map, LOC, structural digest, CI status, test collection. No agents yet.\n2. **Analyze across the 8 dimensions** — (1) code quality, (2) duplication/consolidation, (3) functionality & wiring (trace config→loader→consumer; direction checks), (4) design/UX using `reference/ux-review-overlay.md` when observable surfaces exist, (5) approach vs. the public field, (6) missed opportunities, (7) tools worth integrating, (8) local skills/automations. Bounded, path-scoped, disk-first agents — **offloaded** per `reference/orchestration.md`. Severity tags `[BLOCKER]/[MAJOR]/[MINOR]` (or P0/P1/P2).\n3. **Adversarially verify** each finding against the live tip; drop/`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` the stale ones.\n4. **Prioritize + file** — dedup into one executive report + a cross-cutting prioritized table; file gaps as **AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT** issues (verified `file:line` tasks, a named test gate + deliberate-break→revert, scaffold-forbidden Non-Goals).\n5. **Verification log + reconcile** — maintain the `Code/Audits` repo folder, the repo README there, and the root `AUDIT_LEDGER.md` as the running log (finding → done / deferred-with-reason / declined-with-reason / scheduled); end with a reconciliation pass that proves nothing was silently dropped. This is what lets an audit span sittings.\n\n## After the audit — the follow-up arc is predictable\nEvery audit's follow-up clustered the same way (plan for it; offload what you can):\n- **Implementation** — one PR/issue at a time, often handed to local lanes; **dedup-check before building** (TMP hand-built a kit another agent had already merged).\n- **Implementation-verification loop** — review merged PRs vs. acceptance criteria; expect dropped/closed-unmerged PRs.\n- **Coverage pushback** — the user will challenge whether the issues cover the ambitious dimensions (5/6/7); split epic/roadmap docs vs. 2-week issues.\n- **Ops/incident tangents** that reuse audit context (Render DB expiry, red `main` from golden files, deploy failures).\n- **Verify-before-done** — never close on \"the next cron tick will validate\"; drive end-to-end verification in-session.\n\n## Hard-won gotchas (checklist; details in the reference files)\n- `closed-PR head looks \"stuck\"` → the user closed it; **reopen to force GitHub to sync the head** (≠ a real failure).\n- **Confound-isolation:** when multi-lane changes fail tests, **fix the known CWD/path/env bug FIRST**, then evaluate refactors — don't bisect blame across lanes prematurely (Counter_Risk burned cycles blaming the wrong lane).\n- **Frozen/source dual-mode:** any path-resolution change needs a source-mode AND frozen-mode test matrix before merge (Counter_Risk shipped a `resolve_runtime_path` fix that broke 5 tests + CI).\n- **Lane isolation when an autonomous fleet is active:** use a `/tmp` worktree + keep the orchestrator heartbeat fresh, or the cron fleet hijacks the checkout.\n- **Platform handoff brief** for things you can't verify (Windows/Excel/COM): leave a copy-paste `*_TEST_BRIEF.md` with commands + pass/fail criteria.\n- **CI-pinned linters:** install the repo's pinned ruff/black version; a PR can be green locally and red on the gate (version skew lints the whole tree differently).\n- **Prove-before-delete:** \"dead code\" is often live via `@main` consumers or runtime fetch — verify zero real callers before proposing deletion (the Workflows reusable-CI slim thesis was refuted on verification).\n\n===== /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/audit-storage.md =====\n# Audit Storage Conventions\n\nLoad this before writing any audit artifact. The durable audit root is:\n\n`/Users/teacher/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Audits`\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Keep one folder per audited repo: `Code/Audits/<repo>/`.\n- Treat `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` as the cross-session index and continuity ledger.\n- Treat `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` as the repo-specific index.\n- Prior audit records are continuity and duplicate-check context only. They must not narrow the new audit's category coverage.\n- Keep raw/generated artifacts in the repo folder when small. Link to the canonical artifact path for large packets.\n- Use repo-local `docs/audit/` or `docs/ux-review/` only when the repo intentionally owns an in-repo log. The canonical cross-repo audit record still lives under `Code/Audits`.\n\n## Required Start Steps\n\n1. Read `Code/Audits/README.md`.\n2. Read `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md`.\n3. Read `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` and prior summaries if the repo folder exists.\n4. Create `Code/Audits/<repo>/` if missing.\n5. Start `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-audit-run.md` with:\n\n```text\nrepo:\naudit_id:\nstarted_at:\nbase_branch:\nbase_sha:\nauditor:\nautomation_or_skill:\nprior_context_read:\nscope:\ndeliverables:\ncategories_planned:\nstorage_paths:\nopen_questions:\n```\n\n6. Update `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` with an in-progress row or note before analysis fan-out.\n\n## File Naming\n\nUse date-prefixed files so multiple rounds can coexist:\n\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-scope.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-audit-run.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-00-repo-map.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-NN-<area>.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-UX_REVIEW.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-AUDIT_REPORT.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-verification-log.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-issue-bodies/`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/` for screenshots, JSON bundles, CI logs, and large observed evidence.\n\nFor optional Route-Weight or exploration overlays, also write:\n\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-ROUTE_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-ROUTE_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES.json`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-NON_ACTIONABLE.md`\n\n## Ledger Cadence\n\nUpdate `AUDIT_LEDGER.md` and `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` at:\n\n- audit start\n- audit completion\n- issue filing\n- PR creation\n- merge\n- follow-up verification or durability decision\n\nEach ledger update should record source/automation, category coverage, main findings by category, issue/PR links, non-actionable findings, artifact paths, and next ledger action.\n\n## Repo-Local Logs\n\nSome workflows still require repo-local logs:\n\n- `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md` for UX review log PRs.\n- Existing repo `docs/audit/` logs when the repo already uses them.\n\nWhen creating a repo-local log, keep it concise and link back to the `Code/Audits/<repo>/` artifacts. Do not let repo-local logs replace the durable ledger.\n\n===== /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/orchestration.md =====\n# Orchestration & delegation (PREFER this over the Workflow tool)\n\nYou are the audit lead and token-expensive seat. **Do the thinking and the synthesis; hand off the reading, summarizing, searching, and mechanical edits.** An audit is mostly reading, so most of it should not run in the lead seat. This is why the audit skill prefers the **Orchestrator** over same-family subagents: the Orchestrator routes to cheaper local agents and records outcomes.\n\n## Mechanics\nInvoke the Orchestrator skill or manual, then:\n```\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.cursor/bin:$PATH\"\nO=\"$HOME/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator\"\npython3 \"$O/capacity.py\"                       # assess agent budgets first\npython3 \"$O/dispatcher.py\" offload --agent <gemini|cursor|vibe> --prompt-file <f> --timeout <secs>\n```\n- `offload` = read/summarize/research, result returned (use for audit digests, doc reads, research). Background it (`run_in_background`) to parallelize; `--timeout` caps stalls.\n- `delegate --agent <a> --target <owner/repo#N> --lane <opener|closer> --prompt-file <f>` = a coding task that opens a PR (use for implementation-phase work).\n- Same-family subagents are useful for context isolation, not token savings.\n\n## Capacity economics (spend cheap first)\nFree/unlimited (cursor Auto) → flat-sub (vibe) → metered reasoning seats (codex/claude/gemini) → prepaid-frontier/paygo (cursor frontier, aider) LAST. **gemini** = big-context reads + reasoning continuity, but compute-metered with no reliable reset, so give it substantial work, never trivial work. Run `capacity.py` before routing.\n\n## Delegation map for an audit (what worked across TPP + Counter_Risk)\n| Task | Avoid (expensive) | Prefer (cheap) |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|\n| Inventory / repo map | 20+ code-reading agents | bash: `find`+`wc`, a structural `digest.py` (TODO/dup/complexity), `git` state |\n| Reading transcripts / big docs | Claude reads 64 MB | **gemini offload** with a `jq`/`grep` pre-filter in the prompt (never load whole files) |\n| Duplication | full-file reads | AST/hash equality on the named hotspots the digest flagged |\n| Tests | full suite locally (esp. on Dropbox) | **CI status** (`gh run`), `pytest --collect-only`, one smoke test; dispatch `gh workflow run` for real signal |\n| External research (dims 5–6–7) | — | 3–4 web agents, FS-light (this was consistently GOOD ROI) |\n| UX (dim 4) | code-only inference | `frontend_verify.py` observed flows + screenshots + `ux_review.py` panel and improvement mining |\n| Verify findings | re-audit | one adversarial pass per finding-cluster against a frozen snapshot |\n| Implementation | Claude lead does it all | `delegate` to codex (correctness core) / gemini (parsers/dup) / cursor (UI) lanes |\n| Ops follow-up | browser guessing | HTTP probes (`curl /api/health`) + config diffs FIRST; browser only for auth'd clicks |\n\n## Routing by comparative advantage (observed)\n- **gemini** → biggest reads / big-context digests / reasoning continuity.\n- **codex** → correctness-critical reasoning + multi-step coding.\n- **cursor** → mechanical edits, UI work, and — proven here — reliable read-digests (Auto bucket = cheap).\n- **vibe** → cheap/flat-sub, but **unreliable for digest tasks** (in this very build it returned a preamble and no digest → redirect to cursor). Verify vibe output is non-empty.\n\n## Monitor & redirect (do not fire-and-forget)\n- The harness notifies only on *completion*, not death/stall — so always set `--timeout`, and a stall-watcher for anything the timeout won't catch.\n- **Inspect each result; redirect failures** (kill → re-route to a stronger agent). vibe's empty digest above is the canonical example.\n- **Schema-less Markdown returns** — strict `StructuredOutput` broke ~26/32 subagents in one audit and the deep-research swarm in another. Ask for Markdown.\n- **Cap parallelism (~4–6) and path-scope every prompt.** Uncapped, unscoped fan-out is the WF1 disaster (22 agents → `find` over all of Dropbox → 95 min → 0 output).\n- **Check process load + run the reaper before launching** — leaked agents pile up and get misread as Dropbox/Codex slowness.\n- For runs that must outlive the session, prefer `scheduled-checkin` over an in-session watcher.\n- **codex offload sandbox refuses disk-first writes OUTSIDE `--cwd`** (\"OFFLOAD_INCOMPLETE: cannot write ... outside the configured writable roots\"). So a disk-first prompt telling codex to write to `Code/Audits/...` (Dropbox) fails. Give codex an output path INSIDE `--cwd` (e.g. `./audit-out/<file>.md`) and copy it to the Audits folder yourself. gemini/cursor offloads can write to the Dropbox path directly. (Verified 2026-06-28 Inv-Man-Intake audit.)\n- **Point `--cwd` at a FRESH `git clone` of the remote tip on local disk**, not the Dropbox working copy — the Dropbox HEAD can be an orphaned local commit diverged from `origin/main`, and offload agents reading it audit stale code (the prior route-weight offload did exactly this). Also makes all reads fast.\n\n===== /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/playbook.md =====\n# Standard audit playbook (Phases 1–5) + templates\n\n## Phase 1 — Orient (bash only, NO agents)\nGoal: know the shape before spending. Read `audit-storage.md`, then produce `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-00-repo-map.md` from cheap commands:\n- LOC by subsystem (`find … -name '*.py' | xargs wc -l`, package counts); separate **app code from vendored/synced/infra** (the Phase-0 scope boundary).\n- Structural digest: TODO counts, duplication signatures, complexity hotspots (LOC/branch/arg counts). A small `digest.py` over the tree beats agents reading files.\n- Repo state: branches, default branch (it may NOT be `main` — TMP is `phase-3`), dirty files, recent commits.\n- Build/test reality: `ruff check` / linters (install the **CI-pinned** versions), `pytest --collect-only` (count, don't run yet), **CI status via `gh run list`**.\n- Background a full test run ONLY if cheap + non-Dropbox; otherwise rely on CI. Write its log to disk.\n\n## Phase 2 — Analyze across the 8 dimensions (offloaded, bounded agents)\nSplit into subsystem agents + cross-cutting agents, each path-scoped + disk-first. The 8 dimensions:\n1. Code quality (correctness bugs, dead code, hygiene) — trace edge cases (NaN, mixed-sign, div-by-zero, empty).\n2. Duplication & consolidation (AST/hash equality on digest-flagged hotspots; root-vs-template drift).\n3. Functionality & wiring — **trace config key → loader → consumer**; direction checks (\"tighter limit ⇒ more breaches\"); silent-drop configs (`extra=\"ignore\"`).\n4. Design / UX — use `ux-review-overlay.md` for any observable UI/operator surface; capture rendered evidence, screenshots, driven scenarios, panel/scroll overload, component structure, and mined improvement hints. If no UI exists, record a coverage row explaining why UX is not applicable.\n5. Approach vs. the public field — research briefs (offload to web agents; good ROI).\n6. Missed opportunities — adjacent problems the existing machinery almost solves.\n7. Tools worth integrating — cost/benefit/sketch.\n8. Local skills/automations — efficiency, token-sinks, human-touchpoints.\n\n### Reusable per-agent contract (put in EVERY analysis-agent prompt)\n```\n- Scope: ONLY these paths: <list>. Do NOT read outside them. You are READ-ONLY (no edits, no commits).\n- Baseline (run first): <ruff cmd>, test count, current branch — note anything already broken.\n- Read actual files; cite file:line for every claim; NO speculation.\n- Severity-tag findings: [BLOCKER] (wrong/broken/unsafe), [MAJOR], [MINOR].\n- WRITE findings to Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-NN-<area>.md FIRST.\n- RETURN only a short Markdown index: artifact_path, counts by severity, top 3 findings (one line each). NOT the full text.\n```\nCap concurrent agents ≈4–6; offload per `orchestration.md`.\n\n## Phase 3 — Adversarial verification (before anything is filed)\nFor each candidate finding: re-check against the LIVE tip (the code may already fix it). A finding that \"passes the existing test suite\" is normal for real logic bugs (fixtures are homogeneous) — so verify the LOGIC, not the green check. Drop already-implemented findings or mark `STATUS: INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`. Where possible, a different agent family does the refutation pass (independent eyes).\n\n## Phase 4 — Prioritize + file\n- One synthesis agent dedupes the subreports → `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-AUDIT_REPORT.md` (executive) + a cross-cutting **prioritized table** (P0/P1/P2/P3 with `file:line` + which dimension).\n- Rank severity × effort (S/M/L).\n- File gaps as **AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT** issues (canonical: `Workflows/templates/consumer-repo/docs/AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT.md`): verified `file:line` tasks, a named **test gate** + a **deliberate-break → named-test-fails → revert** demonstration, **scaffold-forbidden Non-Goals**, a **Why** with current `file:line` evidence. No subjective adjectives.\n- Split the ambitious dims (5/6/7): epic/roadmap doc vs. 2-week issues (the user WILL ask whether issues cover them — pre-empt it).\n\n## Phase 5 — Verification log + reconcile\n- Maintain `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-verification-log.md`: every finding → status (done / deferred-with-reason / declined-with-reason / scheduled), with the PR/issue link + a one-line why.\n- This is the cross-session continuity artifact — update it as work lands; it turns \"re-read the whole audit\" into \"diff the log\".\n- Update `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` and `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` at audit start, audit completion, issue filing, PR creation, merge, and follow-up verification.\n- Close out with a **reconciliation pass**: walk the original report's findings + appendix sequence against the log; prove each is done / deferred-with-reason / declined / scheduled / explicitly-optional. Re-verify the security/correctness items live.\n\n## Fix-phase discipline (when the audit moves into implementation)\n- **Regression-test-first** for every BLOCKER: write the failing test, then fix, then targeted pytest.\n- **Dedup-check before building** anything (another agent/PR may already have it).\n- **Confound-isolation**: if multi-lane changes fail tests, fix the known CWD/path/env bug FIRST, then re-evaluate — don't bisect blame prematurely.\n- **Frozen/source (or SQLite/Postgres, macOS/Linux) dual-mode test matrix** for any path/env-sensitive change before merge.\n- **Lane isolation** (`/tmp` worktree + fresh orchestrator heartbeat) when the autonomous cron fleet is active, or it hijacks the checkout.\n- **Platform handoff brief** (`*_TEST_BRIEF.md`) for anything you can't verify here (Windows/Excel/COM/Postgres-prod).\n- **Verify-before-done**: drive end-to-end verification in-session; never close on \"the next cron tick will validate\".\n\n===== /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md =====\n# Repo-distinctive gotchas (living catalog) + Phase-0 probe checklist\n\nLoad this during Phase 0. The per-repo sections are the *known* traps (corroborated by the persistent memories — `trend_*`, `counter_risk_*`, `trip_planner_*`, `lms_*`, `workflows_*`, `lint_ruff_*`). The general checklist is what to ASK about a repo you haven't audited before. **Append a new section each time you audit a new repo.**\n\n## General Phase-0 probe checklist (ask the user + verify cheaply)\n- **Default branch** — may NOT be `main` (TMP = `phase-3`; basing PRs wrong fails with blank-sha).\n- **Lint/format gate** — which tool gates CI (`ruff check`? `black`? line-length?), is it push-only vs PR, and does it lint the WHOLE tree (tests/docs/notebooks)? Install the **CI-pinned** version (skew → green-local/red-gate).\n- **Golden/baseline files** — gitignored or committed? Cross-OS float/encoding drift? Materialize-and-fail-by-design?\n- **Config loading** — silent-drop (`extra=\"ignore\"`)? duplicate-key tolerance? config→loader→consumer actually wired?\n- **Hosting/deploy** — free-tier DB expiry (Render Postgres)? **SQLite-in-CI vs Postgres-in-prod**? PyInstaller frozen-vs-source paths? Windows/COM/Excel?\n- **Sync boundary** — are files synced from an upstream repo (local edits overwritten → route fixes upstream)?\n- **Test fixtures** — homogeneous (hide logic bugs that pass green CI)? env-fragile wall-clock assertions (flaky on slow/Dropbox FS)?\n- **Multi-repo interface contracts** — does this repo pair with another (shared config/persistence)?\n\n## Per-repo known distinctives\n\n### Workflows (system-of-record, 9-repo fleet)\n- Copy-sync to consumers via `.github/sync-manifest.yml`; template-vs-root drift is partly intentional (`health-74`). Fixes go to the SOURCE, then sync.\n- Branch protection requires the **`summary` check-run**, NOT the racy `Gate / gate` status. `action_required` stalls on bot-authored commits → close/reopen to re-trigger.\n- Keepalive = event-loop with **GitHub labels as the control plane**; local opener/closer lanes (Codex↔Claude); WIT syncs from the minimal **integration-repo** template (lacks `agents-80/81` BY DESIGN — not drift).\n- **Prove-before-delete**: reusable-CI looks oversized but inline blocks are \"inlined for consumer compatibility\"; consumers call `@main` so \"zero refs here\" ≠ dead.\n\n### Trend_Model_Project (TMP)\n- Default branch **`phase-3`**. Do NOT run `ruff format` (no line-length config → churns unrelated lines; CI gates only `ruff check`).\n- Pydantic `ConfigDict(extra=\"ignore\")` **silently drops** YAML blocks (ran on defaults). Trace config→consumer.\n- Golden CSVs gitignored by a global `*.csv` rule → CI \"float drift\" that's really missing files (`!tests/baseline/test_golden/*.csv`).\n- Strict dep/import gate (`sync_test_dependencies.py`, `.project_modules.txt`); Streamlit nested-expander crash under `AppTest`; `_load_page` stub pollution leaks DummyStreamlit into sys.modules. `tools/*` synced from Workflows.\n\n### trip-planner / Travel-Plan-Permission (TPP)\n- **Dual-repo** system (planner + policy/permission), vendor-neutral contract; cross-repo smoke scripts.\n- **Render free Postgres deletes ~30 days** → Alembic startup crash-loop. Fix = paid `basic-256mb` in BOTH dashboard and `render.yaml` (Blueprint-managed) + resilient `lifespan()`; \"Hobby\" is a workspace tier, not a DB plan. Verify via alembic log + \"service is live\", no \"degraded\".\n- Dropbox-synced `.venv` = catastrophic I/O (4m29s import, 98% I/O wait) — relocate off-Dropbox. Known flaky `WorkspacePage` deliberate-break test (re-run if no frontend changes).\n\n#### 2026-08-11 paired re-audit update (8 issues filed: TPP #1428-1429, tp #1675-1680)\n- **Dominant defect class = POLICY FAILS OPEN. Two independent mechanisms — probe both.**\n  (1) *Two policy engines, one wired:* `check_trip_plan()` (`policy_api.py:1645`) runs only\n  `PolicyEngine`/`policy.yaml`; `PolicyValidator`/`validation.yaml` (which owns `BUD-001`\n  budget cap `trip_limit:5000` blocking, `DUR-001`) is reachable only via\n  `TripPlan.run_validation()` (`models.py:407`) which has **ZERO production callers**. Worse,\n  `_context_from_plan()` (`policy_api.py:804-848`) never passes `estimated_cost` and\n  `PolicyContext` has **no total-cost field**, so the planner path is *structurally* incapable\n  of a spend check. Runtime: $99,999 vs $5,000 blocking → `status=\"pass\"`, `issues=[]`.\n  (2) *Skip-on-missing/NaN:* blocking rules pass when inputs are absent or non-finite\n  (`policy.py:141-142` fare_comparison, `:172-177` cabin_class, `:312-321` non_reimbursable).\n  **Always test with matched controls** — the rules DO fire with data present; and NaN passes\n  where `-50` fails, proving finiteness gap not intentional skip. `tests/python/test_policy_api.py:266-275`\n  actively **encodes** the fail-open, so CI protects it.\n- **Cross-repo seam is coarsely-correct/semantically-lossy — grep the consumer for each field the\n  producer declares required.** TPP's required `policy_status` (`pass|fail`) occurs **exactly\n  once** in all of trip-planner (`integrations/tpp/client.py:934`, stringified into\n  `organization_context.metadata`) and is never branched on; local verdict defaults\n  `status=\"compliant\"` (`app/services/policy.py:235`), only staleness flips it. Also dropped:\n  typed `booking_requirements` (hard-coded `[]`/`{}` at `client.py:911-924`),\n  `compatible_with_planner_cache` (version incompatibility silently accepted), alternative\n  `title`/`suggested_value` (renamed duplicate model). Mitigating: `policy.py:232` documents\n  the local status as intentionally non-authoritative — lowers severity, doesn't kill the finding.\n- **Production imports the TEST package.** `app/services/scenarios.py:11`\n  `from tests.preferences.fixture_corpus import load_fixture_map`, while `pyproject.toml:51`\n  ships only `[\"scripts*\",\"trip_planner*\"]` → blocking `tests` from `sys.path` makes\n  **`trip_planner.app.main` itself unimportable**. Masked in prod ONLY because `render.yaml:6`\n  uses `pip install -e .` (editable keeps repo root on path). Run the \"import the app with\n  `tests` blocked via `sys.meta_path`\" probe on any repo with test fixtures.\n- **`.tmp/trip_planner.db` is a TRACKED 328KB SQLite binary** and the default DB path is\n  CWD-relative (`persistence/db.py:31`) → booting from repo root mutates a tracked file\n  (grew to 397KB, dirtied `git status`). No `.tmp`/`*.db`/`sqlite` in `.gitignore`. **Set\n  `TRIP_PLANNER_DATABASE_URL` to an absolute out-of-repo path BEFORE booting for a UX pass**,\n  or you will dirty the user's repo (and `preview_start` uses the SESSION cwd, not your clone).\n- **UX: the tab bar lies — measure every tab, don't trust the nav model.** Plan **20,188px/28\n  screens** vs Policy **1,354px/1.9** (15×). Root cause is DUPLICATION, not volume:\n  `WorkspaceBudgetPanel` renders at `WorkspacePage.tsx:1902` (inside `activeTab===\"plan\"`, block\n  at 1782) **and** `:2475`; `WorkspacePolicyPanel` at `:1972` **and** `:2538`. This is why\n  **#1309 + #1332 both closed COMPLETED 2026-06-06 while the file GREW 2,257→2,600** — adding\n  tabs without removing duplicated panels can't shrink Plan. Only the *active* panel mounts, so\n  it's a comprehension cost, not runtime. Policy tab = dead-end empty states, **zero** panel\n  controls, and no TPP request on render → a TPP **outage is indistinguishable from compliant**.\n  Marketing `h1` outranks the trip name on every workspace route (trip title below y=875 on\n  mobile). Mobile: `scrollWidth` 399 vs 375, 51 sub-44px targets, 13×13px `planning-mode` radios.\n- **Verification saves, all four worth repeating:** `trip_planner/orchestration/` (3,592 LOC, 5\n  test files, ZERO production imports) is **BY DESIGN** — closed issue **#960** \"Wire broader\n  orchestration only after the planner/runtime seams are proven\" + in-code note at\n  `workspace.py:2823`. cursor called it its top finding. **Always `gh issue list --state closed`\n  before filing an unwired-module finding in these repos.** Also: cursor's `99999→\"pass\"` repro\n  didn't reproduce as stated (its fixture failed on `fare_evidence` — real finding, wrong repro);\n  doubled API requests are React 18 StrictMode dev-only (`main.tsx:14`); and TP-06 Google Maps is\n  **PARTIAL not OPEN** — no SDK loads but the UI now says \"Schematic preview — not a live map\",\n  which was the actual complaint.\n- **Report-only audits evaporate.** All **11** findings from 2026-07-10 were still open at the\n  2026-08-11 tip because that audit filed nothing and its fixes lived on unmerged `codex/*`\n  branches. Confirm merge-to-`main`, not branch existence.\n- **`agents:format` is auto-added by the repo's own format-guard workflow and is NOT a dispatch\n  trigger** (Renovate's #1384 carries it too). Real dispatch triggers remain `agent:<name>` +\n  `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot`. Don't panic-scan on `^agent`. **BUT** its presence\n  correlates with a guard *failure* comment — check for \"not yet agent-processable\" before\n  assuming it's benign.\n\n#### `AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT.md` is MACHINE-ENFORCED — read past the template or every issue bounces\nThe \"Quick Reference Template\" is the first ~70 lines; the enforced contract is the\n**\"Definition of Ready / Quality Bar\" (§104+) and the \"Pre-submit CHECKLIST\" (§223+)**. Reading\nonly the template got 8 of 11 issues auto-rejected by `agents-issue-format-guard.yml` (triggers\non `opened, edited, reopened, labeled, unlabeled`; comments only on FAILURE, then dispatches the\n\"Agents Issue Optimizer format phase, attempt 1 of 3\"). The literal rules the linter applies:\n- **Tasks are checked PER PHYSICAL LINE.** A wrapped task whose artifact sits on the continuation\n  line reads as \"names no artifact\" → rejected. **Put every task on ONE line with a\n  repo-relative path on that line.** This was the single biggest cause of rejection.\n- **≥3 non-create paths that don't resolve = REJECTED.** Absolute and parent-relative paths\n  \"never count as repository evidence\", so `Code/Audits/...` references must live in\n  Implementation Notes and be written WITHOUT backticks/leading `/` (a backticked\n  `path/x.md` gets parsed as a repo path and counted as missing). A **branch name**\n  (`codex/two-trip-live-canary`) also parses as a path — never put one in Tasks.\n- **Bare filenames get parsed as paths** (`mapSurface.ts`, `policy.yaml`, `googleapis/maps.google`)\n  → always cite the full repo-relative path, and verify it (`WorkspacePolicyPanel` is an **alias**;\n  the real file is `frontend/src/components/workspace/panels/PolicyPanel.tsx`).\n- **Banned adjectives are substring-matched anywhere in Acceptance Criteria** — \"a **clean** venv\"\n  rejected #1675. Banned: clean/nice/good/fast/better/intuitive/polished.\n- **Acceptance Criteria needs a runner token in PROSE, not in a fenced block**: `pytest` /\n  `npm test` / `npx vitest` / `gh workflow run` / `curl` / a `smoke`|`verif` token, or a\n  pytest-style `path.py::test_name`. A `file.test.ts::\"quoted name\"` did NOT register.\n- **Non-Goals MUST carry an issue-specific scaffold clause** phrased \"Scaffold-only completion\n  does NOT count: …is a failure of this issue.\" Generic \"don't cut corners\" fails. I omitted this\n  from all 11 bodies.\n- Also required: a deliberate-break→named-test-fails→revert criterion; `Why` must cite a verified\n  `path:line` and say latent-vs-current-break; `## Scope` is mandatory.\n- **Label sets differ and a bad `--label` ABORTS creation** (no issue is created): TPP has no\n  `testing` and no `priority:*`; trip-planner has both.\n- **Write the linter first.** A ~150-line local checker mirroring these rules\n  (`Code/Audits/trip-planner/2026-08-11-assets/issue_lint.py`) took all 11 bodies from\n  8-rejected to 11-passing in one pass. Run it before every `gh issue create` in this fleet.\n- Label sets DIFFER between the pair: TPP has **no** `testing` and **no** `priority:*` (use\n  `type:policy`, `risk:major`, `validation`, `architecture`, `security`); trip-planner has\n  `priority:high|normal|low`, `testing`. A bad `--label` **aborts** issue creation.\n- Committed junk on `main`: tp has `codex-prompt-{610,622,1052}.md`, `autofix_report_enriched.json`,\n  `pr-569-unresolved-threads.md`, `request.json`; **TPP has files literally named `**Source:**`\n  and `=`** (botched shell redirect). Every Alembic log line prints **twice** on startup\n  (undiagnosed: duplicate invocation vs duplicate handlers).\n- Ops notes: `git clone` of trip-planner failed with `early EOF / invalid index-pack output` —\n  retry with `--depth 200 --single-branch main` + `http.postBuffer`. `uv venv`/`uv pip install`\n  on local disk is fast; both repos install clean. Repo's own `scripts/seed_demo_data.py`\n  (`TRIP_PLANNER_SEED_DEMO=1`) gives a flag-gated synthetic demo account + 2 trips — use it\n  instead of creating an account through the UI. gemini hit its 5h soft budget (9.0/8) after 2\n  large offloads; the `ux_review.py` panel returned **3/4** evaluators (cursor absent) with\n  `consensus_flags` all false — report the missing evaluator, don't call it a 4/4 pass.\n\n### Counter_Risk\n- `black --check --line-length 100` runs **push-only on main** (skips PRs); Makefile uses ruff format (mismatch). Baseline goldens **materialize-and-fail by design** — run once, verify, commit the CSV.\n- **PyInstaller frozen-vs-source path resolution** (`resolve_runtime_path`): frozen → bundle roots; source → absolute `parents[3]`. Test BOTH modes or you break source tests (CWD-dependent).\n- `Runner.xlsm` \"buttons\" are inert cell text (fix = OOXML Form Controls, not VBA); the repo's own test asserts the inert design. UTF-8 BOM + hard-coded column indices in parsers. **Risk-math bugs invisible to green CI** (homogeneous fixtures): mixed-sign HHI, denominator mixing.\n\n### LMS (learning-management-system)\n- **CI tests SQLite; prod is Postgres** → 4 Postgres-only migration bugs (psycopg2-vs-3, `version_num VARCHAR(32)`, 63-char identifier limit, constraint-name doubling). Repro with local Docker `postgres:18` before trusting green CI. (2026-08-01: psycopg3 pin now enforced by a settings validator; full alembic chain verified clean on PG18 + live Render at tip.)\n- FSRS rating-bucket **knife-edge float flips** macOS↔Linux — move the test score OFF the boundary (e.g. 0.92→0.97), don't fiddle float tolerances. (Fixed at 2026-08-01 tip: 0.50/0.85 thresholds, off-boundary fixtures.)\n\n#### 2026-08-01 readiness audit update (after the #181-#206 June fix arc all landed genuine)\n- **Dominant defect class shifted to \"last-mile loop wiring\": pieces exist+tested but the primary paths never call them.** `POST /attempts` + BOTH UI attempt forms never call `schedule_from_attempt` (only rubric scoring does, and it has no UI caller); `apply_remediation_triggers` called only by tests; review queue \"Open attempt\" links to the wrong route (`/app/learner` drops prompt_id, ui/api.py:379). Green CI hides all of it — endpoint tests assert persistence, scheduler tests call the scheduler directly; NO HTTP-level attempt→queue→interval e2e. **Check the seam BETWEEN tested units.**\n- **Deployed identity bootstrap is its own audit target:** `lms auth create-user` creates a User only; `create_learner_for_user` has no prod-mounted caller (learners router only under ENABLE_LOCAL_IDENTITY_ROUTES); UI identity = `?learner_id=` query param defaulting \"learner-1\" with no ownership check and silently-empty rendering for missing learners. Drive Session-B parity (AUTH_REQUIRED=true locally) to observe.\n- **Deploy-layer env-var drift:** render.yaml/deployment.md ship `LLM_DAILY_BUDGET_USD`; code reads `LLM_DAILY_CAP_MICRO_USD` (llm/config.py:74). Grep every render.yaml env key for a src/ consumer.\n- `requirements.lock` is compiled `--extra=dev` (jupyter/debugpy in prod image, 1.79GB). Scheduler is a fixed 1/3/7/14/28 ladder — the repo's own project-plan calls it throwaway scaffolding pending FSRS; py-fsrs drops into the existing `fsrs_adapter` seam (rating 1-4 == py-fsrs Rating).\n- Render deploy is PAID tiers by design (starter web + basic-256mb PG, no 90-day clock) — do NOT flag free-tier expiry here.\n- Offload reliability this run: cursor API unreachable; gemini claimed \"report written\" but wrote nothing (salvage its stdout summary + lead-verify); vibe severity-inflates and had 2/3 majors refuted — verify everything from vibe.\n\n### PAEM (Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model)\n- Ships `.github/reference_packs.json` (exercises the Codex refpack path). Ruff lints the whole tree — a notebook `E402` reddens `main` and blocks every PR (reproduce with the exact CI command, not `ruff check <pkg>`).\n\n### Inv-Man-Intake (manager package intake → priority scoring) — audited 2026-06-20\n- **Inert/unwired config was the dominant defect class** — `config/scoring_weights/*.toml` are loaded+validated ONLY by tests; `compute_score` (`scoring/engine.py:111`) uses a hardcoded `default_weights_by_asset_class()` and `get_weight_set()` has no production caller, so operator weight edits do nothing. `config/model_registry.json` + `config/llm_slots.json` are likewise never read by `src/`. → **Always run an \"inert-config sweep\": for each config file, grep its keys for a production (non-test) consumer.** (Generalizes TMP's `extra=\"ignore\"` silent-drops.)\n- **Real bugs pass green CI because baseline fixtures are homogeneous** — `tests/baseline/catalog.yaml` directional checks cover only 1 of 8 asset classes; scenarios sit in [0.45,0.90] (no floor/ceiling/blocked-zero), which is exactly why the `red_flag_applied = final_score != base_score` float-equality bug (`engine.py:141`) survives. The repo's reverted \"directional baseline checks for non-RAR keys\" commit was the attempt to close this. → **Fixture-homogeneity check: do golden/baseline fixtures span edge cases (floor/ceiling/zero/mixed-sign/all-categories), or just the happy path?**\n- **Hardcoded fallbacks drift from their config** — `v1_smoke.py:222-228` fallback `ThresholdConfig` lists 1 mandatory field vs `config/extraction_thresholds.yaml`'s 3 → silent missed escalations when `threshold_config is None`.\n- Consumer repo (most `.github/` synced from Workflows — exclude from scope); root clutter committed (`codex-prompt-*.md` ×8, `coverage.json`, `pytest-junit.xml`, `Issues.txt`, `.project_modules.txt`) — `.gitignore` has the exact `codex-prompt.md` but not the `*` glob.\n\n#### 2026-06-28 full re-audit update (after #592-602 landed)\n- **The inert-config class is now MOSTLY FIXED; the dominant class shifted to \"no finite/bounds validation at numeric trust boundaries.\"** `scoring/engine.py:168` guards components with `<0/>1` only → **NaN passes** (`base_score=nan`, executed). Same gap in weights, red-flag caps, `performance/metrics.py`, `conflict_resolver.py`, and `extraction/confidence.py` threshold parsing. → **Add a \"finite/bounds sweep\": for every float trust boundary, check `math.isfinite` + range, not just `<0/>1`.** (`explainability.py` already does it — the rest don't.)\n- **#592's \"fix\" is HOLLOW/partial:** `weights_by_asset_class_for(x)` (`weights.py:111-117`) returns a SINGLE-key dict and both prod callers hardcode `\"credit\"` → a non-credit submission **raises ValueError** (executed); 7/8 TOMLs still inert. → When verifying an \"inert-config fix,\" check it wired ALL keys, not just one; run the non-happy path.\n- **ci.yml runs only on `push:[main]` (+ dispatch), NOT on pull_request** (Counter_Risk pattern). PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. So format/test breaks merge clean then redden main — exactly how the route-weight testgen PR left main red on black. Check the CI `on:` triggers, not just that CI exists.\n- **The Dropbox checkout had an ORPHANED local commit (`6c3717f`) not on remote `main`** (`gh api compare` 404). Audit the REMOTE tip — `git clone` fresh to local disk; don't trust the Dropbox working copy's HEAD. (The stale 2026-06-27 route-weight offload audited that orphaned commit w/o gh auth → wrong inert-config findings.)\n- `tools/` LLM stack (`llm_provider.py`, `langchain_client.py`, `llm_registry.py`) + `scripts/langchain/*` + `scripts/ci_*` are **synced from Workflows** (sync-manifest) → LLM-bypass/dead-script findings are upstream scope, not local (WIT false-positive class).\n\n### Manager-Database (institutional manager-intelligence platform) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **~51K LOC. App-local dirs to AUDIT:** `api/ etl/ chains/ alerts/ adapters/ llm/ ui/ web/ embeddings.py diff_holdings.py profiler.py alembic/` + app scripts (`seed_universe`, `resolve_aliases`, `seed_managers`, `build_wasm_demo`, `check_dialect_portability`, `verify_schema_idempotence`). **Synced from Workflows (EXCLUDE):** `tools/*`, `scripts/langchain/*`, and listed `scripts/*` (ci_*, coverage_*, autopilot_*, sync_*, state_fingerprint, reference_packs, orchestrator_skill, reusable_ci_scope, validate_run_contract, aggregate_agent_metrics, api_client). Confirm via `Workflows/.github/sync-manifest.yml`.\n- **`ci.yml` is push:[main]-only (+dispatch), NOT pull_request** (Counter_Risk/Inv-Man pattern); PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. A thin caller to `reusable-10-ci-python.yml@main`.\n- **Dual-dialect DB is the spine: SQLite (`DB_PATH`, CI/tests) vs Postgres (`DB_URL`, prod).** Prod bootstraps via `schema.sql` (compose initdb); CI via `alembic upgrade` on SQLite → **schema.sql ↔ Alembic drift with NO parity gate** (gin index, `documents.embedding`, `chat_feedback.created_at` nullability differ). The mature `scripts/check_dialect_portability.py` gate (#976-1010) catches TOKEN patterns only — it MISSES semantic splits (`INSERT OR REPLACE` identity change vs PG `ON CONFLICT`; idempotency). `schema.sql` has Postgres `CREATE EXTENSION` → not SQLite-loadable.\n- **Observed-UX caught the headline BLOCKER that all tests miss:** `ui/app.py:15` `st.Page(url_path=\"\")` without `default=True` crashes the WHOLE Streamlit operator UI at the pinned `streamlit==1.58.0`. `tests/test_ui_navigation.py` uses a `FakeStreamlit` no-op `Page()` → blind; `make app-smoke` not in CI. The offline twin `web/wasm_app.py:29` already has the `default=True` fix → a drift between two near-identical nav builders. **Lesson: drive the real UI; mocked UI tests hide construction-time errors.**\n- **Dominant correctness class = missing finite/bounds validation** (NaN/inf via raw `float()`) at alerts/activism/conviction/edgar-governor/search trust boundaries — same as Inv-Man-Intake; `<0/>1` guards insufficient, use `math.isfinite`+range.\n- **`scripts/seed_managers.py` is the dialect outlier** — hardcodes Postgres `DB_URL` + `psycopg.connect()` (no SQLite), breaks `make db-seed` locally; everything else routes through `adapters/base.py connect_db()`. ETL also hardcodes `manager_id` while API-created SQLite uses `id` PK (`_manager_id_column` resolver exists but ETL doesn't use it).\n- **Beware the codex auto-pilot `[Audit]` issue stream** — it files [Audit] issues continuously (#1273-1284 on audit day). DEDUP against open issues FIRST (CLAUDE.md incident). Issue format: Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance Criteria/Implementation Notes; labels `bug`, `agent:codex`, `agents:formatted`, `priority:high|normal`, `status: ready`, `testing`; assignee `stranske-automation-bot`.\n- API itself is healthy/well-wired (all routers serve; `UI_OFFLINE=1` routes some modules through `offline_api_imports()` stubs — don't set on a live server). Filed #1297-#1303 (2×P0, 5×P1).\n\n### Pension-Data (pension-report fact extraction/normalize/validate → SQLite/Postgres + offline web workspace) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **Finite/bounds class is the headline (same as Inv-Man-Intake/Manager-Database).** Bare `<0/>1` guards at numeric trust boundaries across `quality/ normalize/ quant/ extract/ provenance/ coverage/` (17 sites). Verified worst case: `quality/confidence.py:43` `_bounded_confidence`=`round(max(0.0,min(1.0,v)),6)` → `min(1.0,nan)==1.0` → **NaN confidence becomes `auto_accept`**, bypassing human review; production-reachable via `ops/document_orchestration.py:1266/1008`. Clamp duplicated ×4 → one finite-aware helper fixes most. Run the `math.isfinite` sweep.\n- **`ci.yml` push:[main]-only; `pr-00-gate.yml` had `format_check:false` while repo formats with BLACK** → unformatted code merges green, reddens main (Inv-Man #703 class). Red-main was NOT version skew (black 26.3.1 & 26.5.1 reformat identically) — it was an unformatted file (#608) + non-enforcing gate. `pr-00-gate` is CUSTOM_GATE/repo-owned (local fix OK).\n- **\"Library-complete, wiring-incomplete\" BY DESIGN — check CLOSED issues before flagging overclaim.** API (`api/app.py`) serves hardcoded fixtures even in `proprietary` mode, mounts only 5 routes (no `include_router` → `routes/sql.py` etc. unreachable → their dialect/bool bugs are LATENT not live); extraction never loaded to DB staging (`persist_staging_core_metrics` test-only). BUT this is an **intentional documented owner decision** (#394 fixture-only labeling, #478/#479/#484 serving arc) — the web app already says \"Demo data — not live\". Don't file overclaim/dead-pipeline as a bug; `gh issue list --state closed` FIRST. `staging_consultant_engagements` = deliberately retained per PR #339 (`test_pr339_investigation_confirms_..._should_remain`) → prove-before-delete.\n- Synced scope large: `scripts/langchain/**` (~12.2k LOC) ~all synced; `tools/` LLM stack synced; 219 manifest entries; `config/model_registry.json`+`llm_slots.json` read only by synced `tools/`. Repo-owned CI is substantial+real (entity-regression, extraction-golden-regression, one-pdf-pilot-golden, postgres-integration, quality-replay/sla, nl-sql-golden, web-cloudflare-pages, mac-desktop-tauri).\n- UX (apps/web, observed + `ux_review.py` 4/4): raw unformatted numbers (`98100000000`), no empty-state, API chip `:8000` ≠ server `:8765`. Mature for stage (provenance/confidence/review-queue/anomaly/golden-eval exist) → dims5-7 net-new = bitemporal, entity-res+Form5500, peer benchmark, Docling/tiered extraction. Filed #635-#642 (`agents:auto-pilot` on #635 only).\n\n### Fine-Art-Archive (personal cultural-heritage image pipeline: museum-API acquire → verify → quality → dedup → e-ink render → meta.json sidecar + FastAPI Companion App) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **TWO halves.** The GitHub repo is a (partly intentional) LIBRARY extraction; the REAL ops+data home is a separate LOCAL workspace `Dropbox/Pictures/Claude Project/` (NOT on GitHub) with its OWN **forked, older** `src/fine_art_archive` (3 newest modules missing, ~24 files differ, NO documented canonical rule), **82 ops scripts** (`acquire*.py`, `aggregate_source_quality.py`, `automation_driver.py`, WACZ, dedup/variant runners) never migrated, the operational data (`art_inventory*.csv` ~4,860 rows / ~920 null artists; `archive_phash_cache.json` 3,301 keys; `operations.log`), and an **orphaned launchd driver** (`com.stranske.fineartarchive.driver.plist`, not loaded, points at Dropbox → TCC-exec block). Audit BOTH halves when asked about \"local elements.\"\n- **The Dropbox working copy HEAD is STALE/diverged** (was `1a72d5a` vs remote `51a09a6`). Same orphaned-HEAD gotcha as Inv-Man-Intake — `git clone` the remote tip to local disk and audit THAT.\n- **Dominant defect class = an ENTIRE SUBSYSTEM with no production effect** (generalizes the inert-config class). `quality/source_quality.py` (~472 LOC) is never wired: `acquisition_flow.py:166` always passes `aggregates = aggregates or {}` (nothing ever loads `config/source_quality.yaml`) → `score_for` returns the same tier-1 prior for every source → `select_source` collapses to \"first candidate.\" 4/4 config surfaces inert (`source_quality.yaml`, `host_registry.yaml`, `sources_seed.yaml`, `known_works/*.yaml`); the aggregator only WRITES the YAML (active-learning loop D009 unclosed). → Run the inert-config sweep AND a \"is this whole module wired into a production caller?\" sweep.\n- **Observed-UX caught what code-reading + green tests miss** (drive the FastAPI Companion App): clicking a manifest work with no staged sidecar → blank panel + tiny \"load failed: 404\" (manifest.csv and staging_sidecars/ are separate, drift-prone sources). `/ratings/summary` shows nothing for real ratings because it only counts the DEPRECATED single-axis `rating`, not the current two-axis `quality`/`fit`. `load_manifest` `@lru_cache` + `_RATINGS_CACHE` module global → process-lifetime stale data (observed: healthz reported 4 ratings for an empty on-disk log). htmx from `unpkg` CDN in an offline-first app.\n- **Companion App security/durability gaps no test covers:** `work_id` used as a path segment with no containment (literal `..` resolves outside STAGING; write-capable via the mutating `subject_action`); hardcoded operator-specific `ART_WORKS_ROOT = /Users/teacher/.../Pictures/Art/works` (`api/main.py:35`) breaks off-machine; non-atomic sidecar read-modify-write; `subject_action` appends the audit event BEFORE validation (false trail on 400); negative/NaN `dwell_seconds` accepted+persisted (verified live; Pydantic `allow_inf_nan` default True).\n- **Adversarial verification killed 2 confident \"BLOCKERs\"** from the gemini numeric pass (proof the step is non-negotiable): FFT-NaN gate bypass REFUTED (division is `high/total if total>0 else 0.0`, input `uint8→float32` always finite → ratio can't be NaN); Floyd-Steinberg \"error runaway/no clipping\" REFUTED (`out` stores quantized palette colors + final `np.clip`; not clamping the working buffer mid-diffusion is textbook FS). Several real numeric items (NaN-sort, hardcoded weights, work-class year parse, aspect threshold) are LATENT behind the never-loaded aggregates → fix in the wiring PR, don't file separately.\n- **Verify stack is honestly STAGED, not buggy** (Pension-Data \"library-complete by design\" lesson): `verify.py:226-239` Layers 3 (CLIP)/4 (VLM) are skip-stubs labeled \"not implemented yet\", default off; Layer 5 missing. Don't file as overclaim. Dim-6: the only ACTIVE identity check (pHash-vs-reference) is the WRONG primary tool — museum-master vs Wikidata/Commons reference differs by crop/frame/color, pHash is luminance-only (can't catch a color-wrong reproduction) → 2026 best practice = DINOv2/CLIP embedding cosine + separate Lab color check (aligns w/ open epic #22).\n- **CI = standard fleet pattern** (`ci.yml` push:[main]-only by explicit design comment — `pull_request:` causes startup_failure w/ `secrets: inherit`; PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml` reusable CI). Coverage gate 25% (a `--collect-only` run shows a misleading 21% import-time number; real execution run clears it). Suite green: 211 pass/9 skip. EXCLUDE synced-from-Workflows: `.github/`, `node_modules/` (356 vendored octokit files COMMITTED), `scripts/{ci_*,autopilot_*,sync_*,coverage_*,reference_packs,reusable_ci_scope,state_fingerprint,validate_*,orchestrator_skill,aggregate_agent_metrics,api_client},langchain/,runner_lib/`. First-party scripts: `finalize_acquisition`, `perceptual_dedupe`, `visual_dedupe`, `propose_subject_tags`, `run_companion_app`.\n- **Issue conventions:** AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT (Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance/Implementation Notes). Labels: `bug`/`enhancement`/`documentation`, `priority:high|normal`, `testing`; routing `agent:codex` + `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot` AUTO-DISPATCH the lane (respect ≤5 opener-PR cap — file for triage WITHOUT them unless the user opts into dispatch). Filed #174-#182 (triage-only).\n\n===== /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/ux-review-overlay.md =====\n# UX Review Overlay\n\nLoad this for audit dimension 4 whenever the repo has any UI, browser app, native app, dashboard, operator workflow, or other user-facing surface. If the repo has no observable UI, write an explicit `not_applicable` coverage row instead of silently skipping UX.\n\nThis overlay brings the substance of `$ux-review` into the repo audit. The rule is observed evidence first: never score usability from code reading alone.\n\n## Iron Rules\n\n1. Observed only: score from rendered browser output, `frontend_verify.py` JSON snapshots, screenshots, driven scenarios, or function-level evidence for native/non-browser surfaces.\n2. Full pass by default: cover every primary surface and core interaction unless the user explicitly scopes a smoke pass.\n3. Mine improvements: run `ux_review.synthesize_improvements(report)` and judge the fix hints. The useful deliverable is the improvement set, not just the score.\n4. Do not auto-route findings: file issues without `agent:*` or `agents:*` labels unless asked.\n5. Review-log PRs must not close findings: avoid `Closes`, `Fixes`, and `Resolves`; reference findings as \"issue N\" instead of bare `#N`.\n6. Do not trust status labels alone: for re-reviews, inspect the closing PR diff, verify the named test/runtime gate, and observe behavior again before marking a finding resolved.\n\n## Focus\n\n- Read `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md` if present and capture the last reviewed SHA.\n- Diff from the last reviewed SHA to `HEAD` to prioritize changed surfaces and likely dependents.\n- For first review or missing log, run a full first review and create the repo-local log only if the user wants the UX log PR.\n- Store the canonical audit UX artifacts under `Code/Audits/<repo>/`.\n\n## Capture\n\nUse the Orchestrator verifier when the surface is browser-observable:\n\n```bash\nexport ORCH=/Users/teacher/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.cursor/bin:$PATH\"\nexport ORCH_FRONTEND_VERIFY_BROWSER_ENDPOINT=\"${ORCH_FRONTEND_VERIFY_BROWSER_ENDPOINT:-http://127.0.0.1:9222}\"\npython3 \"$ORCH/frontend_verify.py\" --doctor --require-browser-endpoint --json\n```\n\nFor Dropbox repos, stage the app on local disk when practical before running a dev server. Enumerate primary surfaces and drive core interactions with repeated `frontend_verify.py` calls:\n\n```bash\npython3 \"$ORCH/frontend_verify.py\" \\\n  --url \"$URL\" \\\n  --assert \"text:<expected>\" \\\n  --assert \"role:<role>[=<name>]\" \\\n  --click-text \"<control>\" \\\n  --then-text \"<expected post-state>\" \\\n  --screenshot \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/<surface>.png\"\n```\n\nMaintain a coverage ledger:\n\n```text\nsurface | driven | observed outcome | evidence path | reason if not driven\n```\n\nBuild `bundle.json` only from observed output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"app\": \"owner/repo\",\n  \"review_id\": \"owner/repo:uxreview:YYYY-MM-DD\",\n  \"url\": \"...\",\n  \"commit\": \"<HEAD SHA>\",\n  \"wired\": {\"ok\": true, \"findings\": []},\n  \"coverage\": [{\"surface\": \"...\", \"driven\": true, \"note\": \"...\"}],\n  \"screens\": [{\"name\": \"...\", \"a11y\": \"...\", \"screenshot_path\": \"...\", \"notes\": \"...\"}],\n  \"scenarios\": [{\"name\": \"...\", \"goal\": \"...\", \"steps\": [{\"action\": \"...\", \"observed\": \"...\"}], \"goal_achieved\": true}],\n  \"help_surfaces\": \"observed labels/help/errors and missing guidance\"\n}\n```\n\n## Panel And Mining\n\nRun the shared panel and improvement synthesis:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nbundle=json.load(open(\"bundle.json\"))\nreport=ux_review.review(bundle, evaluators=[\"claude\",\"codex\",\"cursor\",\"vibe\"], adversary=\"claude\", timeout=420)\nprint(json.dumps(report, indent=2))' | tee report.json\n```\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nreport=json.load(open(\"report.json\"))\nprint(json.dumps(ux_review.synthesize_improvements(report), indent=2))' | tee improvements.json\n```\n\nConfirm every evaluator produced non-empty rubric output under `$ORCH/ux_reviews/<review_id>/`. A zero-byte rubric file is not a pass.\n\nWhen the shared engine records evaluator artifacts through `feedback.py`, keep those artifacts in place and link them from the audit UX report instead of copying large raw outputs.\n\n## Gate And Report\n\nRun the shared gate helper when Gate 1 evidence exists:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nprint(json.dumps(ux_review.gate_decision(json.load(open(\"gate1.json\")), json.load(open(\"report.json\"))), indent=2))' | tee gate.json\n```\n\nReport:\n\n- dimension medians and overall score\n- `gate.json` or, if Gate 1 evidence is unavailable, an explicit gate gap; done requires Gate 1 ok, overall at least 7.0, and no severity-4 blocker\n- consensus flags\n- coverage ledger, including undriven surfaces and reasons\n- corroborated findings with evidence paths\n- accepted and rejected improvement hints\n- `ux_review.cross_repo_patterns()` when available\n\nStore:\n\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-UX_REVIEW.md`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/bundle.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/report.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/improvements.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/gate.json` when produced\n- screenshots and verifier JSON in the same assets folder\n\nIf filing findings, dedupe existing issues first, verify `file:line` targets, and write AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT bodies.\n\nIf creating or appending `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md`, include date, reviewed SHA, coverage ledger, scores and overall gate decision, each finding's disposition, and next-focus list. Do it on a branch/PR and inspect the PR body for forbidden close keywords.\n\nAfter the owner spot-checks a review, record calibration when the engine is available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport ux_review\nux_review.calibrate(\"<review_id>\", \"<owner-verdict>\", \"<note>\")'\n```\n\n## Non-Browser Or Blocked Surfaces\n\nIf the app cannot be driven in this environment, record a coverage ledger row with the blocker and create a handoff brief containing commands, expected screens, pass/fail criteria, and artifact destinations. For native surfaces, use function-level, CLI-backed, `osascript`, `screencapture`, or platform-specific smoke evidence where possible and mark the row `driven:false` only when no runtime observation was possible.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/*.md && sed -n '1,500p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/playbook.md && sed -n '1,500p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/orchestration.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/*.md && sed -n '1,500p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/playbook.md && sed -n '1,500p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/orchestration.md\"","aggregated_output":"      82 /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/audit-storage.md\n      47 /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/orchestration.md\n      55 /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/playbook.md\n     202 /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md\n     134 /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/ux-review-overlay.md\n     520 total\n# Standard audit playbook (Phases 1–5) + templates\n\n## Phase 1 — Orient (bash only, NO agents)\nGoal: know the shape before spending. Read `audit-storage.md`, then produce `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-00-repo-map.md` from cheap commands:\n- LOC by subsystem (`find … -name '*.py' | xargs wc -l`, package counts); separate **app code from vendored/synced/infra** (the Phase-0 scope boundary).\n- Structural digest: TODO counts, duplication signatures, complexity hotspots (LOC/branch/arg counts). A small `digest.py` over the tree beats agents reading files.\n- Repo state: branches, default branch (it may NOT be `main` — TMP is `phase-3`), dirty files, recent commits.\n- Build/test reality: `ruff check` / linters (install the **CI-pinned** versions), `pytest --collect-only` (count, don't run yet), **CI status via `gh run list`**.\n- Background a full test run ONLY if cheap + non-Dropbox; otherwise rely on CI. Write its log to disk.\n\n## Phase 2 — Analyze across the 8 dimensions (offloaded, bounded agents)\nSplit into subsystem agents + cross-cutting agents, each path-scoped + disk-first. The 8 dimensions:\n1. Code quality (correctness bugs, dead code, hygiene) — trace edge cases (NaN, mixed-sign, div-by-zero, empty).\n2. Duplication & consolidation (AST/hash equality on digest-flagged hotspots; root-vs-template drift).\n3. Functionality & wiring — **trace config key → loader → consumer**; direction checks (\"tighter limit ⇒ more breaches\"); silent-drop configs (`extra=\"ignore\"`).\n4. Design / UX — use `ux-review-overlay.md` for any observable UI/operator surface; capture rendered evidence, screenshots, driven scenarios, panel/scroll overload, component structure, and mined improvement hints. If no UI exists, record a coverage row explaining why UX is not applicable.\n5. Approach vs. the public field — research briefs (offload to web agents; good ROI).\n6. Missed opportunities — adjacent problems the existing machinery almost solves.\n7. Tools worth integrating — cost/benefit/sketch.\n8. Local skills/automations — efficiency, token-sinks, human-touchpoints.\n\n### Reusable per-agent contract (put in EVERY analysis-agent prompt)\n```\n- Scope: ONLY these paths: <list>. Do NOT read outside them. You are READ-ONLY (no edits, no commits).\n- Baseline (run first): <ruff cmd>, test count, current branch — note anything already broken.\n- Read actual files; cite file:line for every claim; NO speculation.\n- Severity-tag findings: [BLOCKER] (wrong/broken/unsafe), [MAJOR], [MINOR].\n- WRITE findings to Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-NN-<area>.md FIRST.\n- RETURN only a short Markdown index: artifact_path, counts by severity, top 3 findings (one line each). NOT the full text.\n```\nCap concurrent agents ≈4–6; offload per `orchestration.md`.\n\n## Phase 3 — Adversarial verification (before anything is filed)\nFor each candidate finding: re-check against the LIVE tip (the code may already fix it). A finding that \"passes the existing test suite\" is normal for real logic bugs (fixtures are homogeneous) — so verify the LOGIC, not the green check. Drop already-implemented findings or mark `STATUS: INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`. Where possible, a different agent family does the refutation pass (independent eyes).\n\n## Phase 4 — Prioritize + file\n- One synthesis agent dedupes the subreports → `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-AUDIT_REPORT.md` (executive) + a cross-cutting **prioritized table** (P0/P1/P2/P3 with `file:line` + which dimension).\n- Rank severity × effort (S/M/L).\n- File gaps as **AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT** issues (canonical: `Workflows/templates/consumer-repo/docs/AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT.md`): verified `file:line` tasks, a named **test gate** + a **deliberate-break → named-test-fails → revert** demonstration, **scaffold-forbidden Non-Goals**, a **Why** with current `file:line` evidence. No subjective adjectives.\n- Split the ambitious dims (5/6/7): epic/roadmap doc vs. 2-week issues (the user WILL ask whether issues cover them — pre-empt it).\n\n## Phase 5 — Verification log + reconcile\n- Maintain `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-verification-log.md`: every finding → status (done / deferred-with-reason / declined-with-reason / scheduled), with the PR/issue link + a one-line why.\n- This is the cross-session continuity artifact — update it as work lands; it turns \"re-read the whole audit\" into \"diff the log\".\n- Update `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` and `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` at audit start, audit completion, issue filing, PR creation, merge, and follow-up verification.\n- Close out with a **reconciliation pass**: walk the original report's findings + appendix sequence against the log; prove each is done / deferred-with-reason / declined / scheduled / explicitly-optional. Re-verify the security/correctness items live.\n\n## Fix-phase discipline (when the audit moves into implementation)\n- **Regression-test-first** for every BLOCKER: write the failing test, then fix, then targeted pytest.\n- **Dedup-check before building** anything (another agent/PR may already have it).\n- **Confound-isolation**: if multi-lane changes fail tests, fix the known CWD/path/env bug FIRST, then re-evaluate — don't bisect blame prematurely.\n- **Frozen/source (or SQLite/Postgres, macOS/Linux) dual-mode test matrix** for any path/env-sensitive change before merge.\n- **Lane isolation** (`/tmp` worktree + fresh orchestrator heartbeat) when the autonomous cron fleet is active, or it hijacks the checkout.\n- **Platform handoff brief** (`*_TEST_BRIEF.md`) for anything you can't verify here (Windows/Excel/COM/Postgres-prod).\n- **Verify-before-done**: drive end-to-end verification in-session; never close on \"the next cron tick will validate\".\n# Orchestration & delegation (PREFER this over the Workflow tool)\n\nYou are the audit lead and token-expensive seat. **Do the thinking and the synthesis; hand off the reading, summarizing, searching, and mechanical edits.** An audit is mostly reading, so most of it should not run in the lead seat. This is why the audit skill prefers the **Orchestrator** over same-family subagents: the Orchestrator routes to cheaper local agents and records outcomes.\n\n## Mechanics\nInvoke the Orchestrator skill or manual, then:\n```\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.cursor/bin:$PATH\"\nO=\"$HOME/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator\"\npython3 \"$O/capacity.py\"                       # assess agent budgets first\npython3 \"$O/dispatcher.py\" offload --agent <gemini|cursor|vibe> --prompt-file <f> --timeout <secs>\n```\n- `offload` = read/summarize/research, result returned (use for audit digests, doc reads, research). Background it (`run_in_background`) to parallelize; `--timeout` caps stalls.\n- `delegate --agent <a> --target <owner/repo#N> --lane <opener|closer> --prompt-file <f>` = a coding task that opens a PR (use for implementation-phase work).\n- Same-family subagents are useful for context isolation, not token savings.\n\n## Capacity economics (spend cheap first)\nFree/unlimited (cursor Auto) → flat-sub (vibe) → metered reasoning seats (codex/claude/gemini) → prepaid-frontier/paygo (cursor frontier, aider) LAST. **gemini** = big-context reads + reasoning continuity, but compute-metered with no reliable reset, so give it substantial work, never trivial work. Run `capacity.py` before routing.\n\n## Delegation map for an audit (what worked across TPP + Counter_Risk)\n| Task | Avoid (expensive) | Prefer (cheap) |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|\n| Inventory / repo map | 20+ code-reading agents | bash: `find`+`wc`, a structural `digest.py` (TODO/dup/complexity), `git` state |\n| Reading transcripts / big docs | Claude reads 64 MB | **gemini offload** with a `jq`/`grep` pre-filter in the prompt (never load whole files) |\n| Duplication | full-file reads | AST/hash equality on the named hotspots the digest flagged |\n| Tests | full suite locally (esp. on Dropbox) | **CI status** (`gh run`), `pytest --collect-only`, one smoke test; dispatch `gh workflow run` for real signal |\n| External research (dims 5–6–7) | — | 3–4 web agents, FS-light (this was consistently GOOD ROI) |\n| UX (dim 4) | code-only inference | `frontend_verify.py` observed flows + screenshots + `ux_review.py` panel and improvement mining |\n| Verify findings | re-audit | one adversarial pass per finding-cluster against a frozen snapshot |\n| Implementation | Claude lead does it all | `delegate` to codex (correctness core) / gemini (parsers/dup) / cursor (UI) lanes |\n| Ops follow-up | browser guessing | HTTP probes (`curl /api/health`) + config diffs FIRST; browser only for auth'd clicks |\n\n## Routing by comparative advantage (observed)\n- **gemini** → biggest reads / big-context digests / reasoning continuity.\n- **codex** → correctness-critical reasoning + multi-step coding.\n- **cursor** → mechanical edits, UI work, and — proven here — reliable read-digests (Auto bucket = cheap).\n- **vibe** → cheap/flat-sub, but **unreliable for digest tasks** (in this very build it returned a preamble and no digest → redirect to cursor). Verify vibe output is non-empty.\n\n## Monitor & redirect (do not fire-and-forget)\n- The harness notifies only on *completion*, not death/stall — so always set `--timeout`, and a stall-watcher for anything the timeout won't catch.\n- **Inspect each result; redirect failures** (kill → re-route to a stronger agent). vibe's empty digest above is the canonical example.\n- **Schema-less Markdown returns** — strict `StructuredOutput` broke ~26/32 subagents in one audit and the deep-research swarm in another. Ask for Markdown.\n- **Cap parallelism (~4–6) and path-scope every prompt.** Uncapped, unscoped fan-out is the WF1 disaster (22 agents → `find` over all of Dropbox → 95 min → 0 output).\n- **Check process load + run the reaper before launching** — leaked agents pile up and get misread as Dropbox/Codex slowness.\n- For runs that must outlive the session, prefer `scheduled-checkin` over an in-session watcher.\n- **codex offload sandbox refuses disk-first writes OUTSIDE `--cwd`** (\"OFFLOAD_INCOMPLETE: cannot write ... outside the configured writable roots\"). So a disk-first prompt telling codex to write to `Code/Audits/...` (Dropbox) fails. Give codex an output path INSIDE `--cwd` (e.g. `./audit-out/<file>.md`) and copy it to the Audits folder yourself. gemini/cursor offloads can write to the Dropbox path directly. (Verified 2026-06-28 Inv-Man-Intake audit.)\n- **Point `--cwd` at a FRESH `git clone` of the remote tip on local disk**, not the Dropbox working copy — the Dropbox HEAD can be an orphaned local commit diverged from `origin/main`, and offload agents reading it audit stale code (the prior route-weight offload did exactly this). Also makes all reads fast.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md && sed -n '1,180p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/audit-storage.md && sed -n '1,220p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/ux-review-overlay.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md && sed -n '1,180p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/audit-storage.md && sed -n '1,220p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/ux-review-overlay.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Repo-distinctive gotchas (living catalog) + Phase-0 probe checklist\n\nLoad this during Phase 0. The per-repo sections are the *known* traps (corroborated by the persistent memories — `trend_*`, `counter_risk_*`, `trip_planner_*`, `lms_*`, `workflows_*`, `lint_ruff_*`). The general checklist is what to ASK about a repo you haven't audited before. **Append a new section each time you audit a new repo.**\n\n## General Phase-0 probe checklist (ask the user + verify cheaply)\n- **Default branch** — may NOT be `main` (TMP = `phase-3`; basing PRs wrong fails with blank-sha).\n- **Lint/format gate** — which tool gates CI (`ruff check`? `black`? line-length?), is it push-only vs PR, and does it lint the WHOLE tree (tests/docs/notebooks)? Install the **CI-pinned** version (skew → green-local/red-gate).\n- **Golden/baseline files** — gitignored or committed? Cross-OS float/encoding drift? Materialize-and-fail-by-design?\n- **Config loading** — silent-drop (`extra=\"ignore\"`)? duplicate-key tolerance? config→loader→consumer actually wired?\n- **Hosting/deploy** — free-tier DB expiry (Render Postgres)? **SQLite-in-CI vs Postgres-in-prod**? PyInstaller frozen-vs-source paths? Windows/COM/Excel?\n- **Sync boundary** — are files synced from an upstream repo (local edits overwritten → route fixes upstream)?\n- **Test fixtures** — homogeneous (hide logic bugs that pass green CI)? env-fragile wall-clock assertions (flaky on slow/Dropbox FS)?\n- **Multi-repo interface contracts** — does this repo pair with another (shared config/persistence)?\n\n## Per-repo known distinctives\n\n### Workflows (system-of-record, 9-repo fleet)\n- Copy-sync to consumers via `.github/sync-manifest.yml`; template-vs-root drift is partly intentional (`health-74`). Fixes go to the SOURCE, then sync.\n- Branch protection requires the **`summary` check-run**, NOT the racy `Gate / gate` status. `action_required` stalls on bot-authored commits → close/reopen to re-trigger.\n- Keepalive = event-loop with **GitHub labels as the control plane**; local opener/closer lanes (Codex↔Claude); WIT syncs from the minimal **integration-repo** template (lacks `agents-80/81` BY DESIGN — not drift).\n- **Prove-before-delete**: reusable-CI looks oversized but inline blocks are \"inlined for consumer compatibility\"; consumers call `@main` so \"zero refs here\" ≠ dead.\n\n### Trend_Model_Project (TMP)\n- Default branch **`phase-3`**. Do NOT run `ruff format` (no line-length config → churns unrelated lines; CI gates only `ruff check`).\n- Pydantic `ConfigDict(extra=\"ignore\")` **silently drops** YAML blocks (ran on defaults). Trace config→consumer.\n- Golden CSVs gitignored by a global `*.csv` rule → CI \"float drift\" that's really missing files (`!tests/baseline/test_golden/*.csv`).\n- Strict dep/import gate (`sync_test_dependencies.py`, `.project_modules.txt`); Streamlit nested-expander crash under `AppTest`; `_load_page` stub pollution leaks DummyStreamlit into sys.modules. `tools/*` synced from Workflows.\n\n### trip-planner / Travel-Plan-Permission (TPP)\n- **Dual-repo** system (planner + policy/permission), vendor-neutral contract; cross-repo smoke scripts.\n- **Render free Postgres deletes ~30 days** → Alembic startup crash-loop. Fix = paid `basic-256mb` in BOTH dashboard and `render.yaml` (Blueprint-managed) + resilient `lifespan()`; \"Hobby\" is a workspace tier, not a DB plan. Verify via alembic log + \"service is live\", no \"degraded\".\n- Dropbox-synced `.venv` = catastrophic I/O (4m29s import, 98% I/O wait) — relocate off-Dropbox. Known flaky `WorkspacePage` deliberate-break test (re-run if no frontend changes).\n\n#### 2026-08-11 paired re-audit update (8 issues filed: TPP #1428-1429, tp #1675-1680)\n- **Dominant defect class = POLICY FAILS OPEN. Two independent mechanisms — probe both.**\n  (1) *Two policy engines, one wired:* `check_trip_plan()` (`policy_api.py:1645`) runs only\n  `PolicyEngine`/`policy.yaml`; `PolicyValidator`/`validation.yaml` (which owns `BUD-001`\n  budget cap `trip_limit:5000` blocking, `DUR-001`) is reachable only via\n  `TripPlan.run_validation()` (`models.py:407`) which has **ZERO production callers**. Worse,\n  `_context_from_plan()` (`policy_api.py:804-848`) never passes `estimated_cost` and\n  `PolicyContext` has **no total-cost field**, so the planner path is *structurally* incapable\n  of a spend check. Runtime: $99,999 vs $5,000 blocking → `status=\"pass\"`, `issues=[]`.\n  (2) *Skip-on-missing/NaN:* blocking rules pass when inputs are absent or non-finite\n  (`policy.py:141-142` fare_comparison, `:172-177` cabin_class, `:312-321` non_reimbursable).\n  **Always test with matched controls** — the rules DO fire with data present; and NaN passes\n  where `-50` fails, proving finiteness gap not intentional skip. `tests/python/test_policy_api.py:266-275`\n  actively **encodes** the fail-open, so CI protects it.\n- **Cross-repo seam is coarsely-correct/semantically-lossy — grep the consumer for each field the\n  producer declares required.** TPP's required `policy_status` (`pass|fail`) occurs **exactly\n  once** in all of trip-planner (`integrations/tpp/client.py:934`, stringified into\n  `organization_context.metadata`) and is never branched on; local verdict defaults\n  `status=\"compliant\"` (`app/services/policy.py:235`), only staleness flips it. Also dropped:\n  typed `booking_requirements` (hard-coded `[]`/`{}` at `client.py:911-924`),\n  `compatible_with_planner_cache` (version incompatibility silently accepted), alternative\n  `title`/`suggested_value` (renamed duplicate model). Mitigating: `policy.py:232` documents\n  the local status as intentionally non-authoritative — lowers severity, doesn't kill the finding.\n- **Production imports the TEST package.** `app/services/scenarios.py:11`\n  `from tests.preferences.fixture_corpus import load_fixture_map`, while `pyproject.toml:51`\n  ships only `[\"scripts*\",\"trip_planner*\"]` → blocking `tests` from `sys.path` makes\n  **`trip_planner.app.main` itself unimportable**. Masked in prod ONLY because `render.yaml:6`\n  uses `pip install -e .` (editable keeps repo root on path). Run the \"import the app with\n  `tests` blocked via `sys.meta_path`\" probe on any repo with test fixtures.\n- **`.tmp/trip_planner.db` is a TRACKED 328KB SQLite binary** and the default DB path is\n  CWD-relative (`persistence/db.py:31`) → booting from repo root mutates a tracked file\n  (grew to 397KB, dirtied `git status`). No `.tmp`/`*.db`/`sqlite` in `.gitignore`. **Set\n  `TRIP_PLANNER_DATABASE_URL` to an absolute out-of-repo path BEFORE booting for a UX pass**,\n  or you will dirty the user's repo (and `preview_start` uses the SESSION cwd, not your clone).\n- **UX: the tab bar lies — measure every tab, don't trust the nav model.** Plan **20,188px/28\n  screens** vs Policy **1,354px/1.9** (15×). Root cause is DUPLICATION, not volume:\n  `WorkspaceBudgetPanel` renders at `WorkspacePage.tsx:1902` (inside `activeTab===\"plan\"`, block\n  at 1782) **and** `:2475`; `WorkspacePolicyPanel` at `:1972` **and** `:2538`. This is why\n  **#1309 + #1332 both closed COMPLETED 2026-06-06 while the file GREW 2,257→2,600** — adding\n  tabs without removing duplicated panels can't shrink Plan. Only the *active* panel mounts, so\n  it's a comprehension cost, not runtime. Policy tab = dead-end empty states, **zero** panel\n  controls, and no TPP request on render → a TPP **outage is indistinguishable from compliant**.\n  Marketing `h1` outranks the trip name on every workspace route (trip title below y=875 on\n  mobile). Mobile: `scrollWidth` 399 vs 375, 51 sub-44px targets, 13×13px `planning-mode` radios.\n- **Verification saves, all four worth repeating:** `trip_planner/orchestration/` (3,592 LOC, 5\n  test files, ZERO production imports) is **BY DESIGN** — closed issue **#960** \"Wire broader\n  orchestration only after the planner/runtime seams are proven\" + in-code note at\n  `workspace.py:2823`. cursor called it its top finding. **Always `gh issue list --state closed`\n  before filing an unwired-module finding in these repos.** Also: cursor's `99999→\"pass\"` repro\n  didn't reproduce as stated (its fixture failed on `fare_evidence` — real finding, wrong repro);\n  doubled API requests are React 18 StrictMode dev-only (`main.tsx:14`); and TP-06 Google Maps is\n  **PARTIAL not OPEN** — no SDK loads but the UI now says \"Schematic preview — not a live map\",\n  which was the actual complaint.\n- **Report-only audits evaporate.** All **11** findings from 2026-07-10 were still open at the\n  2026-08-11 tip because that audit filed nothing and its fixes lived on unmerged `codex/*`\n  branches. Confirm merge-to-`main`, not branch existence.\n- **`agents:format` is auto-added by the repo's own format-guard workflow and is NOT a dispatch\n  trigger** (Renovate's #1384 carries it too). Real dispatch triggers remain `agent:<name>` +\n  `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot`. Don't panic-scan on `^agent`. **BUT** its presence\n  correlates with a guard *failure* comment — check for \"not yet agent-processable\" before\n  assuming it's benign.\n\n#### `AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT.md` is MACHINE-ENFORCED — read past the template or every issue bounces\nThe \"Quick Reference Template\" is the first ~70 lines; the enforced contract is the\n**\"Definition of Ready / Quality Bar\" (§104+) and the \"Pre-submit CHECKLIST\" (§223+)**. Reading\nonly the template got 8 of 11 issues auto-rejected by `agents-issue-format-guard.yml` (triggers\non `opened, edited, reopened, labeled, unlabeled`; comments only on FAILURE, then dispatches the\n\"Agents Issue Optimizer format phase, attempt 1 of 3\"). The literal rules the linter applies:\n- **Tasks are checked PER PHYSICAL LINE.** A wrapped task whose artifact sits on the continuation\n  line reads as \"names no artifact\" → rejected. **Put every task on ONE line with a\n  repo-relative path on that line.** This was the single biggest cause of rejection.\n- **≥3 non-create paths that don't resolve = REJECTED.** Absolute and parent-relative paths\n  \"never count as repository evidence\", so `Code/Audits/...` references must live in\n  Implementation Notes and be written WITHOUT backticks/leading `/` (a backticked\n  `path/x.md` gets parsed as a repo path and counted as missing). A **branch name**\n  (`codex/two-trip-live-canary`) also parses as a path — never put one in Tasks.\n- **Bare filenames get parsed as paths** (`mapSurface.ts`, `policy.yaml`, `googleapis/maps.google`)\n  → always cite the full repo-relative path, and verify it (`WorkspacePolicyPanel` is an **alias**;\n  the real file is `frontend/src/components/workspace/panels/PolicyPanel.tsx`).\n- **Banned adjectives are substring-matched anywhere in Acceptance Criteria** — \"a **clean** venv\"\n  rejected #1675. Banned: clean/nice/good/fast/better/intuitive/polished.\n- **Acceptance Criteria needs a runner token in PROSE, not in a fenced block**: `pytest` /\n  `npm test` / `npx vitest` / `gh workflow run` / `curl` / a `smoke`|`verif` token, or a\n  pytest-style `path.py::test_name`. A `file.test.ts::\"quoted name\"` did NOT register.\n- **Non-Goals MUST carry an issue-specific scaffold clause** phrased \"Scaffold-only completion\n  does NOT count: …is a failure of this issue.\" Generic \"don't cut corners\" fails. I omitted this\n  from all 11 bodies.\n- Also required: a deliberate-break→named-test-fails→revert criterion; `Why` must cite a verified\n  `path:line` and say latent-vs-current-break; `## Scope` is mandatory.\n- **Label sets differ and a bad `--label` ABORTS creation** (no issue is created): TPP has no\n  `testing` and no `priority:*`; trip-planner has both.\n- **Write the linter first.** A ~150-line local checker mirroring these rules\n  (`Code/Audits/trip-planner/2026-08-11-assets/issue_lint.py`) took all 11 bodies from\n  8-rejected to 11-passing in one pass. Run it before every `gh issue create` in this fleet.\n- Label sets DIFFER between the pair: TPP has **no** `testing` and **no** `priority:*` (use\n  `type:policy`, `risk:major`, `validation`, `architecture`, `security`); trip-planner has\n  `priority:high|normal|low`, `testing`. A bad `--label` **aborts** issue creation.\n- Committed junk on `main`: tp has `codex-prompt-{610,622,1052}.md`, `autofix_report_enriched.json`,\n  `pr-569-unresolved-threads.md`, `request.json`; **TPP has files literally named `**Source:**`\n  and `=`** (botched shell redirect). Every Alembic log line prints **twice** on startup\n  (undiagnosed: duplicate invocation vs duplicate handlers).\n- Ops notes: `git clone` of trip-planner failed with `early EOF / invalid index-pack output` —\n  retry with `--depth 200 --single-branch main` + `http.postBuffer`. `uv venv`/`uv pip install`\n  on local disk is fast; both repos install clean. Repo's own `scripts/seed_demo_data.py`\n  (`TRIP_PLANNER_SEED_DEMO=1`) gives a flag-gated synthetic demo account + 2 trips — use it\n  instead of creating an account through the UI. gemini hit its 5h soft budget (9.0/8) after 2\n  large offloads; the `ux_review.py` panel returned **3/4** evaluators (cursor absent) with\n  `consensus_flags` all false — report the missing evaluator, don't call it a 4/4 pass.\n\n### Counter_Risk\n- `black --check --line-length 100` runs **push-only on main** (skips PRs); Makefile uses ruff format (mismatch). Baseline goldens **materialize-and-fail by design** — run once, verify, commit the CSV.\n- **PyInstaller frozen-vs-source path resolution** (`resolve_runtime_path`): frozen → bundle roots; source → absolute `parents[3]`. Test BOTH modes or you break source tests (CWD-dependent).\n- `Runner.xlsm` \"buttons\" are inert cell text (fix = OOXML Form Controls, not VBA); the repo's own test asserts the inert design. UTF-8 BOM + hard-coded column indices in parsers. **Risk-math bugs invisible to green CI** (homogeneous fixtures): mixed-sign HHI, denominator mixing.\n\n### LMS (learning-management-system)\n- **CI tests SQLite; prod is Postgres** → 4 Postgres-only migration bugs (psycopg2-vs-3, `version_num VARCHAR(32)`, 63-char identifier limit, constraint-name doubling). Repro with local Docker `postgres:18` before trusting green CI. (2026-08-01: psycopg3 pin now enforced by a settings validator; full alembic chain verified clean on PG18 + live Render at tip.)\n- FSRS rating-bucket **knife-edge float flips** macOS↔Linux — move the test score OFF the boundary (e.g. 0.92→0.97), don't fiddle float tolerances. (Fixed at 2026-08-01 tip: 0.50/0.85 thresholds, off-boundary fixtures.)\n\n#### 2026-08-01 readiness audit update (after the #181-#206 June fix arc all landed genuine)\n- **Dominant defect class shifted to \"last-mile loop wiring\": pieces exist+tested but the primary paths never call them.** `POST /attempts` + BOTH UI attempt forms never call `schedule_from_attempt` (only rubric scoring does, and it has no UI caller); `apply_remediation_triggers` called only by tests; review queue \"Open attempt\" links to the wrong route (`/app/learner` drops prompt_id, ui/api.py:379). Green CI hides all of it — endpoint tests assert persistence, scheduler tests call the scheduler directly; NO HTTP-level attempt→queue→interval e2e. **Check the seam BETWEEN tested units.**\n- **Deployed identity bootstrap is its own audit target:** `lms auth create-user` creates a User only; `create_learner_for_user` has no prod-mounted caller (learners router only under ENABLE_LOCAL_IDENTITY_ROUTES); UI identity = `?learner_id=` query param defaulting \"learner-1\" with no ownership check and silently-empty rendering for missing learners. Drive Session-B parity (AUTH_REQUIRED=true locally) to observe.\n- **Deploy-layer env-var drift:** render.yaml/deployment.md ship `LLM_DAILY_BUDGET_USD`; code reads `LLM_DAILY_CAP_MICRO_USD` (llm/config.py:74). Grep every render.yaml env key for a src/ consumer.\n- `requirements.lock` is compiled `--extra=dev` (jupyter/debugpy in prod image, 1.79GB). Scheduler is a fixed 1/3/7/14/28 ladder — the repo's own project-plan calls it throwaway scaffolding pending FSRS; py-fsrs drops into the existing `fsrs_adapter` seam (rating 1-4 == py-fsrs Rating).\n- Render deploy is PAID tiers by design (starter web + basic-256mb PG, no 90-day clock) — do NOT flag free-tier expiry here.\n- Offload reliability this run: cursor API unreachable; gemini claimed \"report written\" but wrote nothing (salvage its stdout summary + lead-verify); vibe severity-inflates and had 2/3 majors refuted — verify everything from vibe.\n\n### PAEM (Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model)\n- Ships `.github/reference_packs.json` (exercises the Codex refpack path). Ruff lints the whole tree — a notebook `E402` reddens `main` and blocks every PR (reproduce with the exact CI command, not `ruff check <pkg>`).\n\n### Inv-Man-Intake (manager package intake → priority scoring) — audited 2026-06-20\n- **Inert/unwired config was the dominant defect class** — `config/scoring_weights/*.toml` are loaded+validated ONLY by tests; `compute_score` (`scoring/engine.py:111`) uses a hardcoded `default_weights_by_asset_class()` and `get_weight_set()` has no production caller, so operator weight edits do nothing. `config/model_registry.json` + `config/llm_slots.json` are likewise never read by `src/`. → **Always run an \"inert-config sweep\": for each config file, grep its keys for a production (non-test) consumer.** (Generalizes TMP's `extra=\"ignore\"` silent-drops.)\n- **Real bugs pass green CI because baseline fixtures are homogeneous** — `tests/baseline/catalog.yaml` directional checks cover only 1 of 8 asset classes; scenarios sit in [0.45,0.90] (no floor/ceiling/blocked-zero), which is exactly why the `red_flag_applied = final_score != base_score` float-equality bug (`engine.py:141`) survives. The repo's reverted \"directional baseline checks for non-RAR keys\" commit was the attempt to close this. → **Fixture-homogeneity check: do golden/baseline fixtures span edge cases (floor/ceiling/zero/mixed-sign/all-categories), or just the happy path?**\n- **Hardcoded fallbacks drift from their config** — `v1_smoke.py:222-228` fallback `ThresholdConfig` lists 1 mandatory field vs `config/extraction_thresholds.yaml`'s 3 → silent missed escalations when `threshold_config is None`.\n- Consumer repo (most `.github/` synced from Workflows — exclude from scope); root clutter committed (`codex-prompt-*.md` ×8, `coverage.json`, `pytest-junit.xml`, `Issues.txt`, `.project_modules.txt`) — `.gitignore` has the exact `codex-prompt.md` but not the `*` glob.\n\n#### 2026-06-28 full re-audit update (after #592-602 landed)\n- **The inert-config class is now MOSTLY FIXED; the dominant class shifted to \"no finite/bounds validation at numeric trust boundaries.\"** `scoring/engine.py:168` guards components with `<0/>1` only → **NaN passes** (`base_score=nan`, executed). Same gap in weights, red-flag caps, `performance/metrics.py`, `conflict_resolver.py`, and `extraction/confidence.py` threshold parsing. → **Add a \"finite/bounds sweep\": for every float trust boundary, check `math.isfinite` + range, not just `<0/>1`.** (`explainability.py` already does it — the rest don't.)\n- **#592's \"fix\" is HOLLOW/partial:** `weights_by_asset_class_for(x)` (`weights.py:111-117`) returns a SINGLE-key dict and both prod callers hardcode `\"credit\"` → a non-credit submission **raises ValueError** (executed); 7/8 TOMLs still inert. → When verifying an \"inert-config fix,\" check it wired ALL keys, not just one; run the non-happy path.\n- **ci.yml runs only on `push:[main]` (+ dispatch), NOT on pull_request** (Counter_Risk pattern). PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. So format/test breaks merge clean then redden main — exactly how the route-weight testgen PR left main red on black. Check the CI `on:` triggers, not just that CI exists.\n- **The Dropbox checkout had an ORPHANED local commit (`6c3717f`) not on remote `main`** (`gh api compare` 404). Audit the REMOTE tip — `git clone` fresh to local disk; don't trust the Dropbox working copy's HEAD. (The stale 2026-06-27 route-weight offload audited that orphaned commit w/o gh auth → wrong inert-config findings.)\n- `tools/` LLM stack (`llm_provider.py`, `langchain_client.py`, `llm_registry.py`) + `scripts/langchain/*` + `scripts/ci_*` are **synced from Workflows** (sync-manifest) → LLM-bypass/dead-script findings are upstream scope, not local (WIT false-positive class).\n\n### Manager-Database (institutional manager-intelligence platform) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **~51K LOC. App-local dirs to AUDIT:** `api/ etl/ chains/ alerts/ adapters/ llm/ ui/ web/ embeddings.py diff_holdings.py profiler.py alembic/` + app scripts (`seed_universe`, `resolve_aliases`, `seed_managers`, `build_wasm_demo`, `check_dialect_portability`, `verify_schema_idempotence`). **Synced from Workflows (EXCLUDE):** `tools/*`, `scripts/langchain/*`, and listed `scripts/*` (ci_*, coverage_*, autopilot_*, sync_*, state_fingerprint, reference_packs, orchestrator_skill, reusable_ci_scope, validate_run_contract, aggregate_agent_metrics, api_client). Confirm via `Workflows/.github/sync-manifest.yml`.\n- **`ci.yml` is push:[main]-only (+dispatch), NOT pull_request** (Counter_Risk/Inv-Man pattern); PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. A thin caller to `reusable-10-ci-python.yml@main`.\n- **Dual-dialect DB is the spine: SQLite (`DB_PATH`, CI/tests) vs Postgres (`DB_URL`, prod).** Prod bootstraps via `schema.sql` (compose initdb); CI via `alembic upgrade` on SQLite → **schema.sql ↔ Alembic drift with NO parity gate** (gin index, `documents.embedding`, `chat_feedback.created_at` nullability differ). The mature `scripts/check_dialect_portability.py` gate (#976-1010) catches TOKEN patterns only — it MISSES semantic splits (`INSERT OR REPLACE` identity change vs PG `ON CONFLICT`; idempotency). `schema.sql` has Postgres `CREATE EXTENSION` → not SQLite-loadable.\n- **Observed-UX caught the headline BLOCKER that all tests miss:** `ui/app.py:15` `st.Page(url_path=\"\")` without `default=True` crashes the WHOLE Streamlit operator UI at the pinned `streamlit==1.58.0`. `tests/test_ui_navigation.py` uses a `FakeStreamlit` no-op `Page()` → blind; `make app-smoke` not in CI. The offline twin `web/wasm_app.py:29` already has the `default=True` fix → a drift between two near-identical nav builders. **Lesson: drive the real UI; mocked UI tests hide construction-time errors.**\n- **Dominant correctness class = missing finite/bounds validation** (NaN/inf via raw `float()`) at alerts/activism/conviction/edgar-governor/search trust boundaries — same as Inv-Man-Intake; `<0/>1` guards insufficient, use `math.isfinite`+range.\n- **`scripts/seed_managers.py` is the dialect outlier** — hardcodes Postgres `DB_URL` + `psycopg.connect()` (no SQLite), breaks `make db-seed` locally; everything else routes through `adapters/base.py connect_db()`. ETL also hardcodes `manager_id` while API-created SQLite uses `id` PK (`_manager_id_column` resolver exists but ETL doesn't use it).\n- **Beware the codex auto-pilot `[Audit]` issue stream** — it files [Audit] issues continuously (#1273-1284 on audit day). DEDUP against open issues FIRST (CLAUDE.md incident). Issue format: Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance Criteria/Implementation Notes; labels `bug`, `agent:codex`, `agents:formatted`, `priority:high|normal`, `status: ready`, `testing`; assignee `stranske-automation-bot`.\n- API itself is healthy/well-wired (all routers serve; `UI_OFFLINE=1` routes some modules through `offline_api_imports()` stubs — don't set on a live server). Filed #1297-#1303 (2×P0, 5×P1).\n\n### Pension-Data (pension-report fact extraction/normalize/validate → SQLite/Postgres + offline web workspace) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **Finite/bounds class is the headline (same as Inv-Man-Intake/Manager-Database).** Bare `<0/>1` guards at numeric trust boundaries across `quality/ normalize/ quant/ extract/ provenance/ coverage/` (17 sites). Verified worst case: `quality/confidence.py:43` `_bounded_confidence`=`round(max(0.0,min(1.0,v)),6)` → `min(1.0,nan)==1.0` → **NaN confidence becomes `auto_accept`**, bypassing human review; production-reachable via `ops/document_orchestration.py:1266/1008`. Clamp duplicated ×4 → one finite-aware helper fixes most. Run the `math.isfinite` sweep.\n- **`ci.yml` push:[main]-only; `pr-00-gate.yml` had `format_check:false` while repo formats with BLACK** → unformatted code merges green, reddens main (Inv-Man #703 class). Red-main was NOT version skew (black 26.3.1 & 26.5.1 reformat identically) — it was an unformatted file (#608) + non-enforcing gate. `pr-00-gate` is CUSTOM_GATE/repo-owned (local fix OK).\n- **\"Library-complete, wiring-incomplete\" BY DESIGN — check CLOSED issues before flagging overclaim.** API (`api/app.py`) serves hardcoded fixtures even in `proprietary` mode, mounts only 5 routes (no `include_router` → `routes/sql.py` etc. unreachable → their dialect/bool bugs are LATENT not live); extraction never loaded to DB staging (`persist_staging_core_metrics` test-only). BUT this is an **intentional documented owner decision** (#394 fixture-only labeling, #478/#479/#484 serving arc) — the web app already says \"Demo data — not live\". Don't file overclaim/dead-pipeline as a bug; `gh issue list --state closed` FIRST. `staging_consultant_engagements` = deliberately retained per PR #339 (`test_pr339_investigation_confirms_..._should_remain`) → prove-before-delete.\n- Synced scope large: `scripts/langchain/**` (~12.2k LOC) ~all synced; `tools/` LLM stack synced; 219 manifest entries; `config/model_registry.json`+`llm_slots.json` read only by synced `tools/`. Repo-owned CI is substantial+real (entity-regression, extraction-golden-regression, one-pdf-pilot-golden, postgres-integration, quality-replay/sla, nl-sql-golden, web-cloudflare-pages, mac-desktop-tauri).\n- UX (apps/web, observed + `ux_review.py` 4/4): raw unformatted numbers (`98100000000`), no empty-state, API chip `:8000` ≠ server `:8765`. Mature for stage (provenance/confidence/review-queue/anomaly/golden-eval exist) → dims5-7 net-new = bitemporal, entity-res+Form5500, peer benchmark, Docling/tiered extraction. Filed #635-#642 (`agents:auto-pilot` on #635 only).\n\n### Fine-Art-Archive (personal cultural-heritage image pipeline: museum-API acquire → verify → quality → dedup → e-ink render → meta.json sidecar + FastAPI Companion App) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **TWO halves.** The GitHub repo is a (partly intentional) LIBRARY extraction; the REAL ops+data home is a separate LOCAL workspace `Dropbox/Pictures/Claude Project/` (NOT on GitHub) with its OWN **forked, older** `src/fine_art_archive` (3 newest modules missing, ~24 files differ, NO documented canonical rule), **82 ops scripts** (`acquire*.py`, `aggregate_source_quality.py`, `automation_driver.py`, WACZ, dedup/variant runners) never migrated, the operational data (`art_inventory*.csv` ~4,860 rows / ~920 null artists; `archive_phash_cache.json` 3,301 keys; `operations.log`), and an **orphaned launchd driver** (`com.stranske.fineartarchive.driver.plist`, not loaded, points at Dropbox → TCC-exec block). Audit BOTH halves when asked about \"local elements.\"\n- **The Dropbox working copy HEAD is STALE/diverged** (was `1a72d5a` vs remote `51a09a6`). Same orphaned-HEAD gotcha as Inv-Man-Intake — `git clone` the remote tip to local disk and audit THAT.\n- **Dominant defect class = an ENTIRE SUBSYSTEM with no production effect** (generalizes the inert-config class). `quality/source_quality.py` (~472 LOC) is never wired: `acquisition_flow.py:166` always passes `aggregates = aggregates or {}` (nothing ever loads `config/source_quality.yaml`) → `score_for` returns the same tier-1 prior for every source → `select_source` collapses to \"first candidate.\" 4/4 config surfaces inert (`source_quality.yaml`, `host_registry.yaml`, `sources_seed.yaml`, `known_works/*.yaml`); the aggregator only WRITES the YAML (active-learning loop D009 unclosed). → Run the inert-config sweep AND a \"is this whole module wired into a production caller?\" sweep.\n- **Observed-UX caught what code-reading + green tests miss** (drive the FastAPI Companion App): clicking a manifest work with no staged sidecar → blank panel + tiny \"load failed: 404\" (manifest.csv and staging_sidecars/ are separate, drift-prone sources). `/ratings/summary` shows nothing for real ratings because it only counts the DEPRECATED single-axis `rating`, not the current two-axis `quality`/`fit`. `load_manifest` `@lru_cache` + `_RATINGS_CACHE` module global → process-lifetime stale data (observed: healthz reported 4 ratings for an empty on-disk log). htmx from `unpkg` CDN in an offline-first app.\n- **Companion App security/durability gaps no test covers:** `work_id` used as a path segment with no containment (literal `..` resolves outside STAGING; write-capable via the mutating `subject_action`); hardcoded operator-specific `ART_WORKS_ROOT = /Users/teacher/.../Pictures/Art/works` (`api/main.py:35`) breaks off-machine; non-atomic sidecar read-modify-write; `subject_action` appends the audit event BEFORE validation (false trail on 400); negative/NaN `dwell_seconds` accepted+persisted (verified live; Pydantic `allow_inf_nan` default True).\n- **Adversarial verification killed 2 confident \"BLOCKERs\"** from the gemini numeric pass (proof the step is non-negotiable): FFT-NaN gate bypass REFUTED (division is `high/total if total>0 else 0.0`, input `uint8→float32` always finite → ratio can't be NaN); Floyd-Steinberg \"error runaway/no clipping\" REFUTED (`out` stores quantized palette colors + final `np.clip`; not clamping the working buffer mid-diffusion is textbook FS). Several real numeric items (NaN-sort, hardcoded weights, work-class year parse, aspect threshold) are LATENT behind the never-loaded aggregates → fix in the wiring PR, don't file separately.\n- **Verify stack is honestly STAGED, not buggy** (Pension-Data \"library-complete by design\" lesson): `verify.py:226-239` Layers 3 (CLIP)/4 (VLM) are skip-stubs labeled \"not implemented yet\", default off; Layer 5 missing. Don't file as overclaim. Dim-6: the only ACTIVE identity check (pHash-vs-reference) is the WRONG primary tool — museum-master vs Wikidata/Commons reference differs by crop/frame/color, pHash is luminance-only (can't catch a color-wrong reproduction) → 2026 best practice = DINOv2/CLIP embedding cosine + separate Lab color check (aligns w/ open epic #22).\n- **CI = standard fleet pattern** (`ci.yml` push:[main]-only by explicit design comment — `pull_request:` causes startup_failure w/ `secrets: inherit`; PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml` reusable CI). Coverage gate 25% (a `--collect-only` run shows a misleading 21% import-time number; real execution run clears it). Suite green: 211 pass/9 skip. EXCLUDE synced-from-Workflows: `.github/`, `node_modules/` (356 vendored octokit files COMMITTED), `scripts/{ci_*,autopilot_*,sync_*,coverage_*,reference_packs,reusable_ci_scope,state_fingerprint,validate_*,orchestrator_skill,aggregate_agent_metrics,api_client},langchain/,runner_lib/`. First-party scripts: `finalize_acquisition`, `perceptual_dedupe`, `visual_dedupe`, `propose_subject_tags`, `run_companion_app`.\n- **Issue conventions:** AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT (Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance/Implementation Notes). Labels: `bug`/`enhancement`/`documentation`, `priority:high|normal`, `testing`; routing `agent:codex` + `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot` AUTO-DISPATCH the lane (respect ≤5 opener-PR cap — file for triage WITHOUT them unless the user opts into dispatch). Filed #174-#182 (triage-only).\n# Audit Storage Conventions\n\nLoad this before writing any audit artifact. The durable audit root is:\n\n`/Users/teacher/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Audits`\n\n## Core Rules\n\n- Keep one folder per audited repo: `Code/Audits/<repo>/`.\n- Treat `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` as the cross-session index and continuity ledger.\n- Treat `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` as the repo-specific index.\n- Prior audit records are continuity and duplicate-check context only. They must not narrow the new audit's category coverage.\n- Keep raw/generated artifacts in the repo folder when small. Link to the canonical artifact path for large packets.\n- Use repo-local `docs/audit/` or `docs/ux-review/` only when the repo intentionally owns an in-repo log. The canonical cross-repo audit record still lives under `Code/Audits`.\n\n## Required Start Steps\n\n1. Read `Code/Audits/README.md`.\n2. Read `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md`.\n3. Read `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` and prior summaries if the repo folder exists.\n4. Create `Code/Audits/<repo>/` if missing.\n5. Start `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-audit-run.md` with:\n\n```text\nrepo:\naudit_id:\nstarted_at:\nbase_branch:\nbase_sha:\nauditor:\nautomation_or_skill:\nprior_context_read:\nscope:\ndeliverables:\ncategories_planned:\nstorage_paths:\nopen_questions:\n```\n\n6. Update `Code/Audits/AUDIT_LEDGER.md` with an in-progress row or note before analysis fan-out.\n\n## File Naming\n\nUse date-prefixed files so multiple rounds can coexist:\n\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-scope.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-audit-run.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-00-repo-map.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-NN-<area>.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-UX_REVIEW.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-AUDIT_REPORT.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-verification-log.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-issue-bodies/`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/` for screenshots, JSON bundles, CI logs, and large observed evidence.\n\nFor optional Route-Weight or exploration overlays, also write:\n\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-ROUTE_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES.md`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-ROUTE_WEIGHT_CANDIDATES.json`\n- `<YYYY-MM-DD>-NON_ACTIONABLE.md`\n\n## Ledger Cadence\n\nUpdate `AUDIT_LEDGER.md` and `Code/Audits/<repo>/README.md` at:\n\n- audit start\n- audit completion\n- issue filing\n- PR creation\n- merge\n- follow-up verification or durability decision\n\nEach ledger update should record source/automation, category coverage, main findings by category, issue/PR links, non-actionable findings, artifact paths, and next ledger action.\n\n## Repo-Local Logs\n\nSome workflows still require repo-local logs:\n\n- `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md` for UX review log PRs.\n- Existing repo `docs/audit/` logs when the repo already uses them.\n\nWhen creating a repo-local log, keep it concise and link back to the `Code/Audits/<repo>/` artifacts. Do not let repo-local logs replace the durable ledger.\n# UX Review Overlay\n\nLoad this for audit dimension 4 whenever the repo has any UI, browser app, native app, dashboard, operator workflow, or other user-facing surface. If the repo has no observable UI, write an explicit `not_applicable` coverage row instead of silently skipping UX.\n\nThis overlay brings the substance of `$ux-review` into the repo audit. The rule is observed evidence first: never score usability from code reading alone.\n\n## Iron Rules\n\n1. Observed only: score from rendered browser output, `frontend_verify.py` JSON snapshots, screenshots, driven scenarios, or function-level evidence for native/non-browser surfaces.\n2. Full pass by default: cover every primary surface and core interaction unless the user explicitly scopes a smoke pass.\n3. Mine improvements: run `ux_review.synthesize_improvements(report)` and judge the fix hints. The useful deliverable is the improvement set, not just the score.\n4. Do not auto-route findings: file issues without `agent:*` or `agents:*` labels unless asked.\n5. Review-log PRs must not close findings: avoid `Closes`, `Fixes`, and `Resolves`; reference findings as \"issue N\" instead of bare `#N`.\n6. Do not trust status labels alone: for re-reviews, inspect the closing PR diff, verify the named test/runtime gate, and observe behavior again before marking a finding resolved.\n\n## Focus\n\n- Read `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md` if present and capture the last reviewed SHA.\n- Diff from the last reviewed SHA to `HEAD` to prioritize changed surfaces and likely dependents.\n- For first review or missing log, run a full first review and create the repo-local log only if the user wants the UX log PR.\n- Store the canonical audit UX artifacts under `Code/Audits/<repo>/`.\n\n## Capture\n\nUse the Orchestrator verifier when the surface is browser-observable:\n\n```bash\nexport ORCH=/Users/teacher/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Learning/Code/Orchestrator\nexport PATH=\"/opt/homebrew/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.cursor/bin:$PATH\"\nexport ORCH_FRONTEND_VERIFY_BROWSER_ENDPOINT=\"${ORCH_FRONTEND_VERIFY_BROWSER_ENDPOINT:-http://127.0.0.1:9222}\"\npython3 \"$ORCH/frontend_verify.py\" --doctor --require-browser-endpoint --json\n```\n\nFor Dropbox repos, stage the app on local disk when practical before running a dev server. Enumerate primary surfaces and drive core interactions with repeated `frontend_verify.py` calls:\n\n```bash\npython3 \"$ORCH/frontend_verify.py\" \\\n  --url \"$URL\" \\\n  --assert \"text:<expected>\" \\\n  --assert \"role:<role>[=<name>]\" \\\n  --click-text \"<control>\" \\\n  --then-text \"<expected post-state>\" \\\n  --screenshot \"$ARTIFACT_DIR/<surface>.png\"\n```\n\nMaintain a coverage ledger:\n\n```text\nsurface | driven | observed outcome | evidence path | reason if not driven\n```\n\nBuild `bundle.json` only from observed output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"app\": \"owner/repo\",\n  \"review_id\": \"owner/repo:uxreview:YYYY-MM-DD\",\n  \"url\": \"...\",\n  \"commit\": \"<HEAD SHA>\",\n  \"wired\": {\"ok\": true, \"findings\": []},\n  \"coverage\": [{\"surface\": \"...\", \"driven\": true, \"note\": \"...\"}],\n  \"screens\": [{\"name\": \"...\", \"a11y\": \"...\", \"screenshot_path\": \"...\", \"notes\": \"...\"}],\n  \"scenarios\": [{\"name\": \"...\", \"goal\": \"...\", \"steps\": [{\"action\": \"...\", \"observed\": \"...\"}], \"goal_achieved\": true}],\n  \"help_surfaces\": \"observed labels/help/errors and missing guidance\"\n}\n```\n\n## Panel And Mining\n\nRun the shared panel and improvement synthesis:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nbundle=json.load(open(\"bundle.json\"))\nreport=ux_review.review(bundle, evaluators=[\"claude\",\"codex\",\"cursor\",\"vibe\"], adversary=\"claude\", timeout=420)\nprint(json.dumps(report, indent=2))' | tee report.json\n```\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nreport=json.load(open(\"report.json\"))\nprint(json.dumps(ux_review.synthesize_improvements(report), indent=2))' | tee improvements.json\n```\n\nConfirm every evaluator produced non-empty rubric output under `$ORCH/ux_reviews/<review_id>/`. A zero-byte rubric file is not a pass.\n\nWhen the shared engine records evaluator artifacts through `feedback.py`, keep those artifacts in place and link them from the audit UX report instead of copying large raw outputs.\n\n## Gate And Report\n\nRun the shared gate helper when Gate 1 evidence exists:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport json, ux_review\nprint(json.dumps(ux_review.gate_decision(json.load(open(\"gate1.json\")), json.load(open(\"report.json\"))), indent=2))' | tee gate.json\n```\n\nReport:\n\n- dimension medians and overall score\n- `gate.json` or, if Gate 1 evidence is unavailable, an explicit gate gap; done requires Gate 1 ok, overall at least 7.0, and no severity-4 blocker\n- consensus flags\n- coverage ledger, including undriven surfaces and reasons\n- corroborated findings with evidence paths\n- accepted and rejected improvement hints\n- `ux_review.cross_repo_patterns()` when available\n\nStore:\n\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-UX_REVIEW.md`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/bundle.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/report.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/improvements.json`\n- `Code/Audits/<repo>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-assets/gate.json` when produced\n- screenshots and verifier JSON in the same assets folder\n\nIf filing findings, dedupe existing issues first, verify `file:line` targets, and write AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT bodies.\n\nIf creating or appending `docs/ux-review/REVIEW_LOG.md`, include date, reviewed SHA, coverage ledger, scores and overall gate decision, each finding's disposition, and next-focus list. Do it on a branch/PR and inspect the PR body for forbidden close keywords.\n\nAfter the owner spot-checks a review, record calibration when the engine is available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=\"$ORCH\" python3 -c '\nimport ux_review\nux_review.calibrate(\"<review_id>\", \"<owner-verdict>\", \"<note>\")'\n```\n\n## Non-Browser Or Blocked Surfaces\n\nIf the app cannot be driven in this environment, record a coverage ledger row with the blocker and create a handoff brief containing commands, expected screens, pass/fail criteria, and artifact destinations. For native surfaces, use function-level, CLI-backed, `osascript`, `screencapture`, or platform-specific smoke evidence where possible and mark the row `driven:false` only when no runtime observation was possible.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md\nsed -n '111,220p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md\nsed -n '111,220p' /Users/teacher/.claude/skills/repo-audit/reference/repo-distinctives.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Repo-distinctive gotchas (living catalog) + Phase-0 probe checklist\n\nLoad this during Phase 0. The per-repo sections are the *known* traps (corroborated by the persistent memories — `trend_*`, `counter_risk_*`, `trip_planner_*`, `lms_*`, `workflows_*`, `lint_ruff_*`). The general checklist is what to ASK about a repo you haven't audited before. **Append a new section each time you audit a new repo.**\n\n## General Phase-0 probe checklist (ask the user + verify cheaply)\n- **Default branch** — may NOT be `main` (TMP = `phase-3`; basing PRs wrong fails with blank-sha).\n- **Lint/format gate** — which tool gates CI (`ruff check`? `black`? line-length?), is it push-only vs PR, and does it lint the WHOLE tree (tests/docs/notebooks)? Install the **CI-pinned** version (skew → green-local/red-gate).\n- **Golden/baseline files** — gitignored or committed? Cross-OS float/encoding drift? Materialize-and-fail-by-design?\n- **Config loading** — silent-drop (`extra=\"ignore\"`)? duplicate-key tolerance? config→loader→consumer actually wired?\n- **Hosting/deploy** — free-tier DB expiry (Render Postgres)? **SQLite-in-CI vs Postgres-in-prod**? PyInstaller frozen-vs-source paths? Windows/COM/Excel?\n- **Sync boundary** — are files synced from an upstream repo (local edits overwritten → route fixes upstream)?\n- **Test fixtures** — homogeneous (hide logic bugs that pass green CI)? env-fragile wall-clock assertions (flaky on slow/Dropbox FS)?\n- **Multi-repo interface contracts** — does this repo pair with another (shared config/persistence)?\n\n## Per-repo known distinctives\n\n### Workflows (system-of-record, 9-repo fleet)\n- Copy-sync to consumers via `.github/sync-manifest.yml`; template-vs-root drift is partly intentional (`health-74`). Fixes go to the SOURCE, then sync.\n- Branch protection requires the **`summary` check-run**, NOT the racy `Gate / gate` status. `action_required` stalls on bot-authored commits → close/reopen to re-trigger.\n- Keepalive = event-loop with **GitHub labels as the control plane**; local opener/closer lanes (Codex↔Claude); WIT syncs from the minimal **integration-repo** template (lacks `agents-80/81` BY DESIGN — not drift).\n- **Prove-before-delete**: reusable-CI looks oversized but inline blocks are \"inlined for consumer compatibility\"; consumers call `@main` so \"zero refs here\" ≠ dead.\n\n### Trend_Model_Project (TMP)\n- Default branch **`phase-3`**. Do NOT run `ruff format` (no line-length config → churns unrelated lines; CI gates only `ruff check`).\n- Pydantic `ConfigDict(extra=\"ignore\")` **silently drops** YAML blocks (ran on defaults). Trace config→consumer.\n- Golden CSVs gitignored by a global `*.csv` rule → CI \"float drift\" that's really missing files (`!tests/baseline/test_golden/*.csv`).\n- Strict dep/import gate (`sync_test_dependencies.py`, `.project_modules.txt`); Streamlit nested-expander crash under `AppTest`; `_load_page` stub pollution leaks DummyStreamlit into sys.modules. `tools/*` synced from Workflows.\n\n### trip-planner / Travel-Plan-Permission (TPP)\n- **Dual-repo** system (planner + policy/permission), vendor-neutral contract; cross-repo smoke scripts.\n- **Render free Postgres deletes ~30 days** → Alembic startup crash-loop. Fix = paid `basic-256mb` in BOTH dashboard and `render.yaml` (Blueprint-managed) + resilient `lifespan()`; \"Hobby\" is a workspace tier, not a DB plan. Verify via alembic log + \"service is live\", no \"degraded\".\n- Dropbox-synced `.venv` = catastrophic I/O (4m29s import, 98% I/O wait) — relocate off-Dropbox. Known flaky `WorkspacePage` deliberate-break test (re-run if no frontend changes).\n\n#### 2026-08-11 paired re-audit update (8 issues filed: TPP #1428-1429, tp #1675-1680)\n- **Dominant defect class = POLICY FAILS OPEN. Two independent mechanisms — probe both.**\n  (1) *Two policy engines, one wired:* `check_trip_plan()` (`policy_api.py:1645`) runs only\n  `PolicyEngine`/`policy.yaml`; `PolicyValidator`/`validation.yaml` (which owns `BUD-001`\n  budget cap `trip_limit:5000` blocking, `DUR-001`) is reachable only via\n  `TripPlan.run_validation()` (`models.py:407`) which has **ZERO production callers**. Worse,\n  `_context_from_plan()` (`policy_api.py:804-848`) never passes `estimated_cost` and\n  `PolicyContext` has **no total-cost field**, so the planner path is *structurally* incapable\n  of a spend check. Runtime: $99,999 vs $5,000 blocking → `status=\"pass\"`, `issues=[]`.\n  (2) *Skip-on-missing/NaN:* blocking rules pass when inputs are absent or non-finite\n  (`policy.py:141-142` fare_comparison, `:172-177` cabin_class, `:312-321` non_reimbursable).\n  **Always test with matched controls** — the rules DO fire with data present; and NaN passes\n  where `-50` fails, proving finiteness gap not intentional skip. `tests/python/test_policy_api.py:266-275`\n  actively **encodes** the fail-open, so CI protects it.\n- **Cross-repo seam is coarsely-correct/semantically-lossy — grep the consumer for each field the\n  producer declares required.** TPP's required `policy_status` (`pass|fail`) occurs **exactly\n  once** in all of trip-planner (`integrations/tpp/client.py:934`, stringified into\n  `organization_context.metadata`) and is never branched on; local verdict defaults\n  `status=\"compliant\"` (`app/services/policy.py:235`), only staleness flips it. Also dropped:\n  typed `booking_requirements` (hard-coded `[]`/`{}` at `client.py:911-924`),\n  `compatible_with_planner_cache` (version incompatibility silently accepted), alternative\n  `title`/`suggested_value` (renamed duplicate model). Mitigating: `policy.py:232` documents\n  the local status as intentionally non-authoritative — lowers severity, doesn't kill the finding.\n- **Production imports the TEST package.** `app/services/scenarios.py:11`\n  `from tests.preferences.fixture_corpus import load_fixture_map`, while `pyproject.toml:51`\n  ships only `[\"scripts*\",\"trip_planner*\"]` → blocking `tests` from `sys.path` makes\n  **`trip_planner.app.main` itself unimportable**. Masked in prod ONLY because `render.yaml:6`\n  uses `pip install -e .` (editable keeps repo root on path). Run the \"import the app with\n  `tests` blocked via `sys.meta_path`\" probe on any repo with test fixtures.\n- **`.tmp/trip_planner.db` is a TRACKED 328KB SQLite binary** and the default DB path is\n  CWD-relative (`persistence/db.py:31`) → booting from repo root mutates a tracked file\n  (grew to 397KB, dirtied `git status`). No `.tmp`/`*.db`/`sqlite` in `.gitignore`. **Set\n  `TRIP_PLANNER_DATABASE_URL` to an absolute out-of-repo path BEFORE booting for a UX pass**,\n  or you will dirty the user's repo (and `preview_start` uses the SESSION cwd, not your clone).\n- **UX: the tab bar lies — measure every tab, don't trust the nav model.** Plan **20,188px/28\n  screens** vs Policy **1,354px/1.9** (15×). Root cause is DUPLICATION, not volume:\n  `WorkspaceBudgetPanel` renders at `WorkspacePage.tsx:1902` (inside `activeTab===\"plan\"`, block\n  at 1782) **and** `:2475`; `WorkspacePolicyPanel` at `:1972` **and** `:2538`. This is why\n  **#1309 + #1332 both closed COMPLETED 2026-06-06 while the file GREW 2,257→2,600** — adding\n  tabs without removing duplicated panels can't shrink Plan. Only the *active* panel mounts, so\n  it's a comprehension cost, not runtime. Policy tab = dead-end empty states, **zero** panel\n  controls, and no TPP request on render → a TPP **outage is indistinguishable from compliant**.\n  Marketing `h1` outranks the trip name on every workspace route (trip title below y=875 on\n  mobile). Mobile: `scrollWidth` 399 vs 375, 51 sub-44px targets, 13×13px `planning-mode` radios.\n- **Verification saves, all four worth repeating:** `trip_planner/orchestration/` (3,592 LOC, 5\n  test files, ZERO production imports) is **BY DESIGN** — closed issue **#960** \"Wire broader\n  orchestration only after the planner/runtime seams are proven\" + in-code note at\n  `workspace.py:2823`. cursor called it its top finding. **Always `gh issue list --state closed`\n  before filing an unwired-module finding in these repos.** Also: cursor's `99999→\"pass\"` repro\n  didn't reproduce as stated (its fixture failed on `fare_evidence` — real finding, wrong repro);\n  doubled API requests are React 18 StrictMode dev-only (`main.tsx:14`); and TP-06 Google Maps is\n  **PARTIAL not OPEN** — no SDK loads but the UI now says \"Schematic preview — not a live map\",\n  which was the actual complaint.\n- **Report-only audits evaporate.** All **11** findings from 2026-07-10 were still open at the\n  2026-08-11 tip because that audit filed nothing and its fixes lived on unmerged `codex/*`\n  branches. Confirm merge-to-`main`, not branch existence.\n- **`agents:format` is auto-added by the repo's own format-guard workflow and is NOT a dispatch\n  trigger** (Renovate's #1384 carries it too). Real dispatch triggers remain `agent:<name>` +\n  `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot`. Don't panic-scan on `^agent`. **BUT** its presence\n  correlates with a guard *failure* comment — check for \"not yet agent-processable\" before\n  assuming it's benign.\n\n#### `AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT.md` is MACHINE-ENFORCED — read past the template or every issue bounces\nThe \"Quick Reference Template\" is the first ~70 lines; the enforced contract is the\n**\"Definition of Ready / Quality Bar\" (§104+) and the \"Pre-submit CHECKLIST\" (§223+)**. Reading\nonly the template got 8 of 11 issues auto-rejected by `agents-issue-format-guard.yml` (triggers\non `opened, edited, reopened, labeled, unlabeled`; comments only on FAILURE, then dispatches the\n\"Agents Issue Optimizer format phase, attempt 1 of 3\"). The literal rules the linter applies:\n- **Tasks are checked PER PHYSICAL LINE.** A wrapped task whose artifact sits on the continuation\n  line reads as \"names no artifact\" → rejected. **Put every task on ONE line with a\n  repo-relative path on that line.** This was the single biggest cause of rejection.\n- **≥3 non-create paths that don't resolve = REJECTED.** Absolute and parent-relative paths\n  \"never count as repository evidence\", so `Code/Audits/...` references must live in\n  Implementation Notes and be written WITHOUT backticks/leading `/` (a backticked\n  `path/x.md` gets parsed as a repo path and counted as missing). A **branch name**\n  (`codex/two-trip-live-canary`) also parses as a path — never put one in Tasks.\n- **Bare filenames get parsed as paths** (`mapSurface.ts`, `policy.yaml`, `googleapis/maps.google`)\n  → always cite the full repo-relative path, and verify it (`WorkspacePolicyPanel` is an **alias**;\n  the real file is `frontend/src/components/workspace/panels/PolicyPanel.tsx`).\n- **Banned adjectives are substring-matched anywhere in Acceptance Criteria** — \"a **clean** venv\"\n  rejected #1675. Banned: clean/nice/good/fast/better/intuitive/polished.\n- **Acceptance Criteria needs a runner token in PROSE, not in a fenced block**: `pytest` /\n  `npm test` / `npx vitest` / `gh workflow run` / `curl` / a `smoke`|`verif` token, or a\n  pytest-style `path.py::test_name`. A `file.test.ts::\"quoted name\"` did NOT register.\n- **Non-Goals MUST carry an issue-specific scaffold clause** phrased \"Scaffold-only completion\n  does NOT count: …is a failure of this issue.\" Generic \"don't cut corners\" fails. I omitted this\n  from all 11 bodies.\n- Also required: a deliberate-break→named-test-fails→revert criterion; `Why` must cite a verified\n  `path:line` and say latent-vs-current-break; `## Scope` is mandatory.\n- **Label sets differ and a bad `--label` ABORTS creation** (no issue is created): TPP has no\n  `testing` and no `priority:*`; trip-planner has both.\n- **Write the linter first.** A ~150-line local checker mirroring these rules\n  (`Code/Audits/trip-planner/2026-08-11-assets/issue_lint.py`) took all 11 bodies from\n  8-rejected to 11-passing in one pass. Run it before every `gh issue create` in this fleet.\n- Label sets DIFFER between the pair: TPP has **no** `testing` and **no** `priority:*` (use\n  `type:policy`, `risk:major`, `validation`, `architecture`, `security`); trip-planner has\n  `priority:high|normal|low`, `testing`. A bad `--label` **aborts** issue creation.\n- Committed junk on `main`: tp has `codex-prompt-{610,622,1052}.md`, `autofix_report_enriched.json`,\n  `pr-569-unresolved-threads.md`, `request.json`; **TPP has files literally named `**Source:**`\n  and `=`** (botched shell redirect). Every Alembic log line prints **twice** on startup\n  (undiagnosed: duplicate invocation vs duplicate handlers).\n- Ops notes: `git clone` of trip-planner failed with `early EOF / invalid index-pack output` —\n  retry with `--depth 200 --single-branch main` + `http.postBuffer`. `uv venv`/`uv pip install`\n  on local disk is fast; both repos install clean. Repo's own `scripts/seed_demo_data.py`\n  (`TRIP_PLANNER_SEED_DEMO=1`) gives a flag-gated synthetic demo account + 2 trips — use it\n  instead of creating an account through the UI. gemini hit its 5h soft budget (9.0/8) after 2\n  large offloads; the `ux_review.py` panel returned **3/4** evaluators (cursor absent) with\n  `consensus_flags` all false — report the missing evaluator, don't call it a 4/4 pass.\n\n### Counter_Risk\n- `black --check --line-length 100` runs **push-only on main** (skips PRs); Makefile uses ruff format (mismatch). Baseline goldens **materialize-and-fail by design** — run once, verify, commit the CSV.\n- **PyInstaller frozen-vs-source path resolution** (`resolve_runtime_path`): frozen → bundle roots; source → absolute `parents[3]`. Test BOTH modes or you break source tests (CWD-dependent).\n- `Runner.xlsm` \"buttons\" are inert cell text (fix = OOXML Form Controls, not VBA); the repo's own test asserts the inert design. UTF-8 BOM + hard-coded column indices in parsers. **Risk-math bugs invisible to green CI** (homogeneous fixtures): mixed-sign HHI, denominator mixing.\n\n### LMS (learning-management-system)\n- **CI tests SQLite; prod is Postgres** → 4 Postgres-only migration bugs (psycopg2-vs-3, `version_num VARCHAR(32)`, 63-char identifier limit, constraint-name doubling). Repro with local Docker `postgres:18` before trusting green CI. (2026-08-01: psycopg3 pin now enforced by a settings validator; full alembic chain verified clean on PG18 + live Render at tip.)\n- FSRS rating-bucket **knife-edge float flips** macOS↔Linux — move the test score OFF the boundary (e.g. 0.92→0.97), don't fiddle float tolerances. (Fixed at 2026-08-01 tip: 0.50/0.85 thresholds, off-boundary fixtures.)\n\n#### 2026-08-01 readiness audit update (after the #181-#206 June fix arc all landed genuine)\n- **Dominant defect class shifted to \"last-mile loop wiring\": pieces exist+tested but the primary paths never call them.** `POST /attempts` + BOTH UI attempt forms never call `schedule_from_attempt` (only rubric scoring does, and it has no UI caller); `apply_remediation_triggers` called only by tests; review queue \"Open attempt\" links to the wrong route (`/app/learner` drops prompt_id, ui/api.py:379). Green CI hides all of it — endpoint tests assert persistence, scheduler tests call the scheduler directly; NO HTTP-level attempt→queue→interval e2e. **Check the seam BETWEEN tested units.**\n- **Deployed identity bootstrap is its own audit target:** `lms auth create-user` creates a User only; `create_learner_for_user` has no prod-mounted caller (learners router only under ENABLE_LOCAL_IDENTITY_ROUTES); UI identity = `?learner_id=` query param defaulting \"learner-1\" with no ownership check and silently-empty rendering for missing learners. Drive Session-B parity (AUTH_REQUIRED=true locally) to observe.\n- **Deploy-layer env-var drift:** render.yaml/deployment.md ship `LLM_DAILY_BUDGET_USD`; code reads `LLM_DAILY_CAP_MICRO_USD` (llm/config.py:74). Grep every render.yaml env key for a src/ consumer.\n- `requirements.lock` is compiled `--extra=dev` (jupyter/debugpy in prod image, 1.79GB). Scheduler is a fixed 1/3/7/14/28 ladder — the repo's own project-plan calls it throwaway scaffolding pending FSRS; py-fsrs drops into the existing `fsrs_adapter` seam (rating 1-4 == py-fsrs Rating).\n- Render deploy is PAID tiers by design (starter web + basic-256mb PG, no 90-day clock) — do NOT flag free-tier expiry here.\n- Offload reliability this run: cursor API unreachable; gemini claimed \"report written\" but wrote nothing (salvage its stdout summary + lead-verify); vibe severity-inflates and had 2/3 majors refuted — verify everything from vibe.\n\n### PAEM (Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model)\n- Ships `.github/reference_packs.json` (exercises the Codex refpack path). Ruff lints the whole tree — a notebook `E402` reddens `main` and blocks every PR (reproduce with the exact CI command, not `ruff check <pkg>`).\n\n### Inv-Man-Intake (manager package intake → priority scoring) — audited 2026-06-20\n- **Inert/unwired config was the dominant defect class** — `config/scoring_weights/*.toml` are loaded+validated ONLY by tests; `compute_score` (`scoring/engine.py:111`) uses a hardcoded `default_weights_by_asset_class()` and `get_weight_set()` has no production caller, so operator weight edits do nothing. `config/model_registry.json` + `config/llm_slots.json` are likewise never read by `src/`. → **Always run an \"inert-config sweep\": for each config file, grep its keys for a production (non-test) consumer.** (Generalizes TMP's `extra=\"ignore\"` silent-drops.)\n- **Real bugs pass green CI because baseline fixtures are homogeneous** — `tests/baseline/catalog.yaml` directional checks cover only 1 of 8 asset classes; scenarios sit in [0.45,0.90] (no floor/ceiling/blocked-zero), which is exactly why the `red_flag_applied = final_score != base_score` float-equality bug (`engine.py:141`) survives. The repo's reverted \"directional baseline checks for non-RAR keys\" commit was the attempt to close this. → **Fixture-homogeneity check: do golden/baseline fixtures span edge cases (floor/ceiling/zero/mixed-sign/all-categories), or just the happy path?**\n- **Hardcoded fallbacks drift from their config** — `v1_smoke.py:222-228` fallback `ThresholdConfig` lists 1 mandatory field vs `config/extraction_thresholds.yaml`'s 3 → silent missed escalations when `threshold_config is None`.\n- Consumer repo (most `.github/` synced from Workflows — exclude from scope); root clutter committed (`codex-prompt-*.md` ×8, `coverage.json`, `pytest-junit.xml`, `Issues.txt`, `.project_modules.txt`) — `.gitignore` has the exact `codex-prompt.md` but not the `*` glob.\n\n#### 2026-06-28 full re-audit update (after #592-602 landed)\n- **The inert-config class is now MOSTLY FIXED; the dominant class shifted to \"no finite/bounds validation at numeric trust boundaries.\"** `scoring/engine.py:168` guards components with `<0/>1` only → **NaN passes** (`base_score=nan`, executed). Same gap in weights, red-flag caps, `performance/metrics.py`, `conflict_resolver.py`, and `extraction/confidence.py` threshold parsing. → **Add a \"finite/bounds sweep\": for every float trust boundary, check `math.isfinite` + range, not just `<0/>1`.** (`explainability.py` already does it — the rest don't.)\n- **#592's \"fix\" is HOLLOW/partial:** `weights_by_asset_class_for(x)` (`weights.py:111-117`) returns a SINGLE-key dict and both prod callers hardcode `\"credit\"` → a non-credit submission **raises ValueError** (executed); 7/8 TOMLs still inert. → When verifying an \"inert-config fix,\" check it wired ALL keys, not just one; run the non-happy path.\n- **ci.yml runs only on `push:[main]` (+ dispatch), NOT on pull_request** (Counter_Risk pattern). PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. So format/test breaks merge clean then redden main — exactly how the route-weight testgen PR left main red on black. Check the CI `on:` triggers, not just that CI exists.\n- **The Dropbox checkout had an ORPHANED local commit (`6c3717f`) not on remote `main`** (`gh api compare` 404). Audit the REMOTE tip — `git clone` fresh to local disk; don't trust the Dropbox working copy's HEAD. (The stale 2026-06-27 route-weight offload audited that orphaned commit w/o gh auth → wrong inert-config findings.)\n- `tools/` LLM stack (`llm_provider.py`, `langchain_client.py`, `llm_registry.py`) + `scripts/langchain/*` + `scripts/ci_*` are **synced from Workflows** (sync-manifest) → LLM-bypass/dead-script findings are upstream scope, not local (WIT false-positive class).\n\n### Manager-Database (institutional manager-intelligence platform) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **~51K LOC. App-local dirs to AUDIT:** `api/ etl/ chains/ alerts/ adapters/ llm/ ui/ web/ embeddings.py diff_holdings.py profiler.py alembic/` + app scripts (`seed_universe`, `resolve_aliases`, `seed_managers`, `build_wasm_demo`, `check_dialect_portability`, `verify_schema_idempotence`). **Synced from Workflows (EXCLUDE):** `tools/*`, `scripts/langchain/*`, and listed `scripts/*` (ci_*, coverage_*, autopilot_*, sync_*, state_fingerprint, reference_packs, orchestrator_skill, reusable_ci_scope, validate_run_contract, aggregate_agent_metrics, api_client). Confirm via `Workflows/.github/sync-manifest.yml`.\n- **`ci.yml` is push:[main]-only (+dispatch), NOT pull_request** (Counter_Risk/Inv-Man pattern); PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml`. A thin caller to `reusable-10-ci-python.yml@main`.\n- **Dual-dialect DB is the spine: SQLite (`DB_PATH`, CI/tests) vs Postgres (`DB_URL`, prod).** Prod bootstraps via `schema.sql` (compose initdb); CI via `alembic upgrade` on SQLite → **schema.sql ↔ Alembic drift with NO parity gate** (gin index, `documents.embedding`, `chat_feedback.created_at` nullability differ). The mature `scripts/check_dialect_portability.py` gate (#976-1010) catches TOKEN patterns only — it MISSES semantic splits (`INSERT OR REPLACE` identity change vs PG `ON CONFLICT`; idempotency). `schema.sql` has Postgres `CREATE EXTENSION` → not SQLite-loadable.\n- **Observed-UX caught the headline BLOCKER that all tests miss:** `ui/app.py:15` `st.Page(url_path=\"\")` without `default=True` crashes the WHOLE Streamlit operator UI at the pinned `streamlit==1.58.0`. `tests/test_ui_navigation.py` uses a `FakeStreamlit` no-op `Page()` → blind; `make app-smoke` not in CI. The offline twin `web/wasm_app.py:29` already has the `default=True` fix → a drift between two near-identical nav builders. **Lesson: drive the real UI; mocked UI tests hide construction-time errors.**\n- **Dominant correctness class = missing finite/bounds validation** (NaN/inf via raw `float()`) at alerts/activism/conviction/edgar-governor/search trust boundaries — same as Inv-Man-Intake; `<0/>1` guards insufficient, use `math.isfinite`+range.\n- **`scripts/seed_managers.py` is the dialect outlier** — hardcodes Postgres `DB_URL` + `psycopg.connect()` (no SQLite), breaks `make db-seed` locally; everything else routes through `adapters/base.py connect_db()`. ETL also hardcodes `manager_id` while API-created SQLite uses `id` PK (`_manager_id_column` resolver exists but ETL doesn't use it).\n- **Beware the codex auto-pilot `[Audit]` issue stream** — it files [Audit] issues continuously (#1273-1284 on audit day). DEDUP against open issues FIRST (CLAUDE.md incident). Issue format: Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance Criteria/Implementation Notes; labels `bug`, `agent:codex`, `agents:formatted`, `priority:high|normal`, `status: ready`, `testing`; assignee `stranske-automation-bot`.\n- API itself is healthy/well-wired (all routers serve; `UI_OFFLINE=1` routes some modules through `offline_api_imports()` stubs — don't set on a live server). Filed #1297-#1303 (2×P0, 5×P1).\n\n### Pension-Data (pension-report fact extraction/normalize/validate → SQLite/Postgres + offline web workspace) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **Finite/bounds class is the headline (same as Inv-Man-Intake/Manager-Database).** Bare `<0/>1` guards at numeric trust boundaries across `quality/ normalize/ quant/ extract/ provenance/ coverage/` (17 sites). Verified worst case: `quality/confidence.py:43` `_bounded_confidence`=`round(max(0.0,min(1.0,v)),6)` → `min(1.0,nan)==1.0` → **NaN confidence becomes `auto_accept`**, bypassing human review; production-reachable via `ops/document_orchestration.py:1266/1008`. Clamp duplicated ×4 → one finite-aware helper fixes most. Run the `math.isfinite` sweep.\n- **`ci.yml` push:[main]-only; `pr-00-gate.yml` had `format_check:false` while repo formats with BLACK** → unformatted code merges green, reddens main (Inv-Man #703 class). Red-main was NOT version skew (black 26.3.1 & 26.5.1 reformat identically) — it was an unformatted file (#608) + non-enforcing gate. `pr-00-gate` is CUSTOM_GATE/repo-owned (local fix OK).\n- **\"Library-complete, wiring-incomplete\" BY DESIGN — check CLOSED issues before flagging overclaim.** API (`api/app.py`) serves hardcoded fixtures even in `proprietary` mode, mounts only 5 routes (no `include_router` → `routes/sql.py` etc. unreachable → their dialect/bool bugs are LATENT not live); extraction never loaded to DB staging (`persist_staging_core_metrics` test-only). BUT this is an **intentional documented owner decision** (#394 fixture-only labeling, #478/#479/#484 serving arc) — the web app already says \"Demo data — not live\". Don't file overclaim/dead-pipeline as a bug; `gh issue list --state closed` FIRST. `staging_consultant_engagements` = deliberately retained per PR #339 (`test_pr339_investigation_confirms_..._should_remain`) → prove-before-delete.\n- Synced scope large: `scripts/langchain/**` (~12.2k LOC) ~all synced; `tools/` LLM stack synced; 219 manifest entries; `config/model_registry.json`+`llm_slots.json` read only by synced `tools/`. Repo-owned CI is substantial+real (entity-regression, extraction-golden-regression, one-pdf-pilot-golden, postgres-integration, quality-replay/sla, nl-sql-golden, web-cloudflare-pages, mac-desktop-tauri).\n- UX (apps/web, observed + `ux_review.py` 4/4): raw unformatted numbers (`98100000000`), no empty-state, API chip `:8000` ≠ server `:8765`. Mature for stage (provenance/confidence/review-queue/anomaly/golden-eval exist) → dims5-7 net-new = bitemporal, entity-res+Form5500, peer benchmark, Docling/tiered extraction. Filed #635-#642 (`agents:auto-pilot` on #635 only).\n\n### Fine-Art-Archive (personal cultural-heritage image pipeline: museum-API acquire → verify → quality → dedup → e-ink render → meta.json sidecar + FastAPI Companion App) — audited 2026-06-28\n- **TWO halves.** The GitHub repo is a (partly intentional) LIBRARY extraction; the REAL ops+data home is a separate LOCAL workspace `Dropbox/Pictures/Claude Project/` (NOT on GitHub) with its OWN **forked, older** `src/fine_art_archive` (3 newest modules missing, ~24 files differ, NO documented canonical rule), **82 ops scripts** (`acquire*.py`, `aggregate_source_quality.py`, `automation_driver.py`, WACZ, dedup/variant runners) never migrated, the operational data (`art_inventory*.csv` ~4,860 rows / ~920 null artists; `archive_phash_cache.json` 3,301 keys; `operations.log`), and an **orphaned launchd driver** (`com.stranske.fineartarchive.driver.plist`, not loaded, points at Dropbox → TCC-exec block). Audit BOTH halves when asked about \"local elements.\"\n- **The Dropbox working copy HEAD is STALE/diverged** (was `1a72d5a` vs remote `51a09a6`). Same orphaned-HEAD gotcha as Inv-Man-Intake — `git clone` the remote tip to local disk and audit THAT.\n- **Dominant defect class = an ENTIRE SUBSYSTEM with no production effect** (generalizes the inert-config class). `quality/source_quality.py` (~472 LOC) is never wired: `acquisition_flow.py:166` always passes `aggregates = aggregates or {}` (nothing ever loads `config/source_quality.yaml`) → `score_for` returns the same tier-1 prior for every source → `select_source` collapses to \"first candidate.\" 4/4 config surfaces inert (`source_quality.yaml`, `host_registry.yaml`, `sources_seed.yaml`, `known_works/*.yaml`); the aggregator only WRITES the YAML (active-learning loop D009 unclosed). → Run the inert-config sweep AND a \"is this whole module wired into a production caller?\" sweep.\n- **Observed-UX caught what code-reading + green tests miss** (drive the FastAPI Companion App): clicking a manifest work with no staged sidecar → blank panel + tiny \"load failed: 404\" (manifest.csv and staging_sidecars/ are separate, drift-prone sources). `/ratings/summary` shows nothing for real ratings because it only counts the DEPRECATED single-axis `rating`, not the current two-axis `quality`/`fit`. `load_manifest` `@lru_cache` + `_RATINGS_CACHE` module global → process-lifetime stale data (observed: healthz reported 4 ratings for an empty on-disk log). htmx from `unpkg` CDN in an offline-first app.\n- **Companion App security/durability gaps no test covers:** `work_id` used as a path segment with no containment (literal `..` resolves outside STAGING; write-capable via the mutating `subject_action`); hardcoded operator-specific `ART_WORKS_ROOT = /Users/teacher/.../Pictures/Art/works` (`api/main.py:35`) breaks off-machine; non-atomic sidecar read-modify-write; `subject_action` appends the audit event BEFORE validation (false trail on 400); negative/NaN `dwell_seconds` accepted+persisted (verified live; Pydantic `allow_inf_nan` default True).\n- **Adversarial verification killed 2 confident \"BLOCKERs\"** from the gemini numeric pass (proof the step is non-negotiable): FFT-NaN gate bypass REFUTED (division is `high/total if total>0 else 0.0`, input `uint8→float32` always finite → ratio can't be NaN); Floyd-Steinberg \"error runaway/no clipping\" REFUTED (`out` stores quantized palette colors + final `np.clip`; not clamping the working buffer mid-diffusion is textbook FS). Several real numeric items (NaN-sort, hardcoded weights, work-class year parse, aspect threshold) are LATENT behind the never-loaded aggregates → fix in the wiring PR, don't file separately.\n- **Verify stack is honestly STAGED, not buggy** (Pension-Data \"library-complete by design\" lesson): `verify.py:226-239` Layers 3 (CLIP)/4 (VLM) are skip-stubs labeled \"not implemented yet\", default off; Layer 5 missing. Don't file as overclaim. Dim-6: the only ACTIVE identity check (pHash-vs-reference) is the WRONG primary tool — museum-master vs Wikidata/Commons reference differs by crop/frame/color, pHash is luminance-only (can't catch a color-wrong reproduction) → 2026 best practice = DINOv2/CLIP embedding cosine + separate Lab color check (aligns w/ open epic #22).\n- **CI = standard fleet pattern** (`ci.yml` push:[main]-only by explicit design comment — `pull_request:` causes startup_failure w/ `secrets: inherit`; PRs gated by `pr-00-gate.yml` reusable CI). Coverage gate 25% (a `--collect-only` run shows a misleading 21% import-time number; real execution run clears it). Suite green: 211 pass/9 skip. EXCLUDE synced-from-Workflows: `.github/`, `node_modules/` (356 vendored octokit files COMMITTED), `scripts/{ci_*,autopilot_*,sync_*,coverage_*,reference_packs,reusable_ci_scope,state_fingerprint,validate_*,orchestrator_skill,aggregate_agent_metrics,api_client},langchain/,runner_lib/`. First-party scripts: `finalize_acquisition`, `perceptual_dedupe`, `visual_dedupe`, `propose_subject_tags`, `run_companion_app`.\n- **Issue conventions:** AGENT_ISSUE_FORMAT (Why/Scope/Non-Goals/Tasks/Acceptance/Implementation Notes). Labels: `bug`/`enhancement`/`documentation`, `priority:high|normal`, `testing`; routing `agent:codex` + `status:ready` + `agents:auto-pilot` AUTO-DISPATCH the lane (respect ≤5 opener-PR cap — file for triage WITHOUT them unless the user opts into dispatch). Filed #174-#182 (triage-only).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
