{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"out=/Users/teacher/.codex/automations/research-program/artifacts/audits/paem-20260907\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- scope ---'\ncat \\\"\"'$out/scope.md\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- closed dedup issues ---'\njq -r '.[] | select((.number|tostring) as \"'$n | [\"1904\",\"1909\",\"1910\",\"1911\",\"1912\",\"1913\",\"1914\",\"1915\",\"1916\",\"1917\",\"1918\",\"1919\",\"1924\"] | index($n)) | \"#'\"\\\\(.number) [\\\\(.state)] \\\\(.title)\\\\n\\\\(.body // \\\"\\\")\\\\n---\\\"' \\\"\"'$out/issues.json\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- open matching numeric candidates ---'\njq -r '.[] | select(.state==\\\"OPEN\\\") | select((.title+\\\" \\\"+(.body//\\\"\\\")) | test(\\\"sweep|fee|simulation|covariance|config|sleeve|numeric\\\"; \\\"i\\\")) | \\\"#\\\\(.number) \\\\(.title)\\\"' \\\"\"'$out/issues.json\" | head -80'","aggregated_output":"--- scope ---\n# PAEM audit scope\nUnit: D-audit-Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model--2026-09-07T04-47-31Z\nStarted: 2026-09-07T05:13:54.121796+00:00\nBase: main 59cb12be9d4b06434d41bc1b71612167ea6d9cfc\nScope from dossier and owner notes: first-party pa_core, dashboard, web, packaging scripts, tests and repo-owned CI. Synced Workflows infrastructure is upstream-owned. Research and staged issue bodies only; no issue filing or code changes. Eight dimensions planned with explicit coverage limits. Native work Python available; WASM unknown. Synthetic inputs only.\nOrientation: pa_core 165 files/24768 lines; dashboard 21/6343; tests 198/32527; scripts 60/26044. Hotspots cli.py 2106, config.py 1280, sleeve_suggestor.py 1160. Remote current-head CI 34015303572 success. Untracked dossier-out/ pre-exists. System Python numeric ABI errors; isolated uv runtime being installed. Load 24.28,30.37,32.90; no stale ownership established, no unrelated processes killed.\n--- closed dedup issues ---\n#1924 [CLOSED] Active-share is a linear, constant-IR alpha multiplier — the model cannot answer \"how much extension is optimal\"\n[academic research + code] `ActiveExtensionAgent.monthly_returns` ([active_ext.py:13-16](../../../pa_core/agents/active_ext.py)) computes the alpha contribution as `(beta_share × active_share) × r_E` — i.e. `active_share` linearly scales the **whole** extension-alpha stream, both its mean and its volatility. Consequence: the **information ratio of the active bet is invariant to active_share**, so raising active share always raises expected alpha proportionally with **no diminishing returns**. This contradicts the active-extension literature the work will be judged against — Clarke/de Silva/Sapra/Thorley, *\"Long/Short Extensions: How Much Is Enough?\"*, and the Grinold-Kahn fundamental law (IR ≈ TC·IC·√BR): relaxing the long-only constraint raises the **transfer coefficient with diminishing returns**, there is an **interior optimal extension**, and beyond it marginal alpha < marginal cost/risk. As written, a sweep over `active_share` always favors \"more,\" which is the wrong conclusion for the central decision an active-extension model exists to inform. The same linear-scalar pattern applies to `theta_extpa`.\n\n**This is a design defect, not just a documentation gap** (the plumbing is correctly wired — the *economics* of the lever are wrong for its implied purpose). Resolution depends on intent:\n- If `active_share` is the **extension-sizing lever** (\"how much should we run?\"): replace the linear scalar with a transfer-coefficient mapping where TC (hence IR) **declines** as active_share rises, plus a cost/capacity term — yielding an interior optimum. **Fix required before presenting \"optimal extension\" conclusions.**\n- If `active_share` is only a **bet-size multiplier on a pre-calibrated alpha** (user supplies skill-consistent `mu_E`/`sigma_E`): rename/document it as such and hard-scope the tool so it is never used to choose the extension level.\n\n**Decision needed from the owner:** which of the two is intended? That determines fix-vs-scope.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1919 [CLOSED] Robustness edge cases produce NaN / ZeroDivisionError (verified)\nQuality scan found small but real defects: `annualised_return` returns NaN / raises `RuntimeWarning` when mean compounded return < −1 (`metrics.py:139`); `annualised_vol` returns NaN for a single observation (`metrics.py:149`); `total_fund_capital` lacks a `gt=0` constraint → `ZeroDivisionError` in the agent-compile validator at capital 0 (`config.py:261`); `spike_prob`/`financing_sigma` fields lack `ge/le` bounds. All are one-line guards/Field constraints.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1918 [CLOSED] Fix multi-figure PDF export (PyPDF2 → pypdf)\n[C26] `pdf_report.py` writes only the first figure when PyPDF2 is absent (deprecated; unavailable on Py3.12+). Migrate to `pypdf` and ensure all figures are merged; warn if the merge backend is missing. Also fix chart mislabels [C27] (`fan.py` \"Return\" vs cumulative; `corr_heatmap` axes labeled \"Month\").\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1917 [CLOSED] Reuse vetted OSS instead of hand-rolled numerics; add MC error & optimization\n[Item 5] Consider `sklearn.covariance` Ledoit-Wolf (vs the in-house normal-moment approximation), skfolio copulas, and empyrical metrics. Add a **Monte-Carlo standard error / CVaR confidence interval** and a convergence-vs-N diagnostic (board outputs currently look more precise than they are), and consider a parameter-uncertainty/Bayesian layer. Optionally add CVaR/TE-constrained allocation optimization (Riskfolio-Lib/skfolio) to complement the existing sleeve suggestor.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1916 [CLOSED] Document advisory/unwired fields and overlay semantics\n[C13] `risk_metrics` is advisory (doesn't select computed metrics); [C14] `Scenario.sleeves` is validated but unwired (engine reads `ModelConfig`); [C5] beta-sleeve financing is floored at 0 (no positive carry) while internal-PA isn't; [C15] `analysis_mode='single_with_sensitivity'` crashes/degrades on the sweep path. Document each (or wire/guard `single_with_sensitivity`).\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1915 [CLOSED] Config round-trip silently drops convenience-field edits\n[C17] After `model_dump()`, re-applying a tweak to `active_share`/`w_beta_H`/`w_alpha_H`/`theta_extpa` is silently ignored because the compiled `agents` list shadows the convenience fields. Any LLM/config-patch round-trip is exposed. Fix `compile_agent_config` so convenience-field edits on a re-loaded config take effect (or recompile agents when they change).\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1914 [CLOSED] Expose median/percentile terminal return; reconsider TE estimator\n[C9] `terminal_AnnReturn` annualizes the arithmetic mean of compounded terminals (E[wealth], ~6.19%) vs the median CAGR (~4.6%) a typical outcome resembles — expose median + P10/P90. [C8] `monthly_TE` pools all (path×month) active returns (≈2.4% higher than a per-path average); document the definition and optionally offer per-path TE.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1913 [CLOSED] Regime sigma overrides bypass unit normalization\n[C12] `RegimeConfig.sigma_H/E/M` overrides are not run through the annual→monthly conversion that central inputs get, so annual regime sigmas reach the covariance build unconverted (12×/√12 too large) in regime runs. Normalize regime sigma overrides through the same unit policy.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1912 [CLOSED] Annual→monthly mean conversion default doesn't reproduce the annual mean after compounding\n[C10] `DEFAULT_MEAN_CONVERSION='simple'` (`mean/12`) means the configured annual mean is not reproduced once monthly returns compound. Default to geometric `(1+r)^(1/12)-1`, or surface a `mean_conversion` config field and document the choice.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1911 [CLOSED] Financing spike parameters are inert when financing vol is zero\n[C6] `*_spike_prob`/`*_spike_factor` scale jumps by the matching `*_financing_sigma_month`, which defaults to 0 — so a user calibrating a financing-stress scenario with spikes but no vol gets a silent no-op. Add a `model_validator` that warns/errors when any `*_spike_prob>0` or `*_spike_factor>0` while the matching `*_financing_sigma_month==0`.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1910 [CLOSED] Regime-switching is silently ignored in parameter sweeps (verified High)\n[C16] `run_sweep` does not build/apply regime parameters; regimes are honored only in `run_single`. Empirically a 2-regime sweep produced results identical to a no-regime sweep (max abs diff ~0 across all 81 combinations). Since sweeps are the dominant workflow for exploring capital/return/vol grids, an analyst who configures crisis regimes and runs a sweep silently gets no regime effect. Recommend: wire regime support into `run_sweep` mirroring `run_single`, or **refuse to run a sweep when regimes are configured** with a clear error.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1909 [CLOSED] `financing_mode='broadcast'` understates financing-cost risk (verified High)\n[C7] The shipped default `broadcast` reuses a **single** financing path across all Monte-Carlo simulations, so financing-cost dispersion (and any return/financing co-movement) is suppressed — tail/CVaR understated for any run with non-zero financing vol. `per_path` mode exists but is off by default. Recommend: make `per_path` the default for risk/tail analysis (or flip the shipped template), and elevate the `broadcast` notice from a debug log to a visible UI/CLI warning.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n#1904 [CLOSED] Add a management/performance fee & transaction-cost layer\nThe engine models financing/margin cost but has no fee layer. For portable alpha, external-manager fees (and perf fees with hurdles) and turnover/transaction costs are first-order and often decide whether the structure beats plain beta. Without them, all outputs are **gross** and overstate the structure. Add a per-sleeve fee schedule (mgmt bps on notional + perf fee on alpha above a hurdle) so net-of-fee comparisons are possible.\n\n---\n_Filed from the 2026-06-13 whole-repo audit — see `docs/reports/repo-audit-2026-06-13/REPORT.md`._\n---\n--- open matching numeric candidates ---\n#2273 Raise test coverage toward 90% (autopilot round 6, low blast radius only)\n#1958 Dependency Dashboard\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
